-It gets tough.

997
00:39:41,445 --> 00:39:43,080
You're down to about eight minutes.

998
00:39:43,147 --> 00:39:44,615
Seven minutes have gone by.

999
00:39:44,682 --> 00:39:48,352
Nam-no chops scallions into thin slices.

1000
00:39:48,419 --> 00:39:49,687
Those are so thin.

1001
00:39:49,754 --> 00:39:50,755
Very thin.

1002
00:39:50,821 --> 00:39:52,323
What are those for?

1003
00:39:52,390 --> 00:39:54,525
-Toppings?
-Do they have to be so thin?

1004
00:39:54,592 --> 00:39:55,793
It's for the salad.

1005
00:39:55,860 --> 00:39:58,729
-Salad? Oh, the cold dish?
-The cold dish.

1006
00:39:59,630 --> 00:40:00,898
SCALLION, CHEONGYANG PEPPER

1007
00:40:00,965 --> 00:40:03,501
Ho-young preps the morning glory.

1008
00:40:03,934 --> 00:40:05,936
AND HE MINCES THE GARLIC…

1009
00:40:06,637 --> 00:40:09,507
Wait, he's chopping like Poong.

1010
00:40:09,573 --> 00:40:11,575
People do that in Southeast Asia…

1011
00:40:11,642 --> 00:40:14,145
-Yes.
-…to bring out the texture.

1012
00:40:14,211 --> 00:40:17,281
-Into uneven pieces.
-I think it's done for the texture.

1013
00:40:17,348 --> 00:40:18,616
OYSTER SAUCE

1014
00:40:18,682 --> 00:40:20,951
These will be the topping.

1015
00:40:21,018 --> 00:40:22,953
He cooks morning glory with garlic.

1016
00:40:23,020 --> 00:40:24,054
Morning glory stir-fry?

1017
00:40:24,121 --> 00:40:26,824
I guess he's making
a char-grilled style dish.

1018
00:40:26,891 --> 00:40:28,726
-Classic.
-Yes, it's the classic.

1019
00:40:29,460 --> 00:40:30,761
WHAT'S THIS?

1020
00:40:30,828 --> 00:40:34,064
Chef Nam-no picked up the tomato juice.

1021
00:40:34,131 --> 00:40:36,467
The tomato juice. What's it for?

1022
00:40:37,234 --> 00:40:38,436
Soy sauce?

1023
00:40:39,003 --> 00:40:40,471
Tomato juice and soy sauce?

1024
00:40:40,538 --> 00:40:41,405
What?

1025
00:40:42,540 --> 00:40:45,509
-I've never seen that before.
-For the cold salad?

1026
00:40:45,576 --> 00:40:47,211
-Sesame oil?
-<i>Aekjeot</i>, fish sauce.

1027
00:40:47,278 --> 00:40:48,379
<i>-Aekjeot.</i>
<i>-Aekjeot?</i>

1028
00:40:48,446 --> 00:40:49,747
<i>-Aekjeot.</i>
<i>-Aekjeot?</i>

1029
00:40:49,814 --> 00:40:50,981
-Sugar?
-Sugar?

1030
00:40:51,048 --> 00:40:54,018
That must be the sour offal dish
he had mentioned.

1031
00:40:54,885 --> 00:40:56,587
He'll probably mix it with offal.

1032
00:40:58,989 --> 00:41:01,258
-What's that? Spinal cord?
-Spinal cord!

1033
00:41:01,325 --> 00:41:02,393
Beef spinal cord.

1034
00:41:02,460 --> 00:41:03,627
A jump rope.

1035
00:41:04,295 --> 00:41:05,663
I thought it'd go around his neck.

1036
00:41:06,564 --> 00:41:08,265
It's long enough to jump over.

1037
00:41:08,332 --> 00:41:09,800
I thought you were skipping rope.

1038
00:41:09,867 --> 00:41:12,236
That spinal cord looks so nice and chewy.

1039
00:41:12,303 --> 00:41:14,538
-It has to be especially fresh to eat.
-Exactly.

1040
00:41:14,605 --> 00:41:16,173
-You must love beef spinal cord.
-Yes.

1041
00:41:16,240 --> 00:41:18,576
He was very curious to see
how that dish would turn out.

1042
00:41:18,642 --> 00:41:22,379
He's scraping the pollack roe.

1043
00:41:22,446 --> 00:41:24,682
Pollack roe and beef spinal cord.

1044
00:41:24,748 --> 00:41:28,419
-He's mixing them.
-He's mixing them to make a cold dish.

1045
00:41:28,486 --> 00:41:31,922
