TOP WITH CHWINAMUL AND CHEONGYANG PEPPER

1172
00:45:55,552 --> 00:45:57,454
It's boiling. It looks so good.

1173
00:45:57,521 --> 00:45:58,622
One minute.

1174
00:45:58,689 --> 00:46:01,458
The timer has turned red.

1175
00:46:01,525 --> 00:46:03,961
Look at this. Nam-no is almost done too.

1176
00:46:04,027 --> 00:46:06,130
Can you taste his <i>jeongol</i> again?

1177
00:46:06,196 --> 00:46:07,297
It looks good.

1178
00:46:07,364 --> 00:46:10,100
This is insane.
How do they do this? Whoa.

1179
00:46:10,167 --> 00:46:13,103
This is Nam-no's dish
with only 40 seconds left.

1180
00:46:13,170 --> 00:46:14,404
Forty seconds left!

1181
00:46:14,471 --> 00:46:17,040
What's Nam-no's dish like?

1182
00:46:17,107 --> 00:46:17,941
HO-YOUNG FINISHES UP TOO

1183
00:46:18,008 --> 00:46:20,611
-Do you want to save that taste?
-Those two look similar.

1184
00:46:20,677 --> 00:46:22,412
TOPPING 2: SEASONED SPINAL CORD

1185
00:46:22,980 --> 00:46:25,983
CHECKING NAM-NO'S SOUP

1186
00:46:26,583 --> 00:46:28,085
There's a bit of a smell.

1187
00:46:28,152 --> 00:46:30,587
-There's a smell?
-Do you mind strong aromas?

1188
00:46:30,654 --> 00:46:32,823
-Ho-young finishes!
-When did you finish?

1189
00:46:32,890 --> 00:46:34,491
And Nam-no's done too!

1190
00:46:34,725 --> 00:46:36,693
YOON NAM-NO, JUNG HO-YOUNG

1191
00:46:36,760 --> 00:46:38,529
Whoa. When did they finish?

1192
00:46:38,595 --> 00:46:41,532
They both finished
with more than 20 seconds left.

1193
00:46:41,799 --> 00:46:43,400
WHOA…

1194
00:46:43,467 --> 00:46:45,602
Great job. That was fun.

1195
00:46:46,403 --> 00:46:47,604
<i>Jeongol</i> versus <i>jeongol</i>.

1196
00:46:47,671 --> 00:46:49,773
SERVE HIS MAJESTY'S MEALS!

1197
00:46:50,207 --> 00:46:53,043
ALL EYES ON THE DISHES

1198
00:46:53,911 --> 00:46:57,414
HALF AIR, HALF SMELL

1199
00:46:58,015 --> 00:47:02,186
All offal dishes
have been made for Hang-jun.

1200
00:47:02,252 --> 00:47:03,287
-Wow.
-Any thoughts?

1201
00:47:03,353 --> 00:47:06,156
It feels completely different
from watching this on the screen.

1202
00:47:06,223 --> 00:47:09,226
They do everything so smoothly,
yet I can still sense the urgency,

1203
00:47:09,293 --> 00:47:11,395
and on top of that, I can smell things.

1204
00:47:11,461 --> 00:47:13,263
My mouth kept watering,

1205
00:47:13,330 --> 00:47:15,332
so I just couldn't wait.

1206
00:47:15,399 --> 00:47:17,901
Please try Chef Ho-young's dish first.

1207
00:47:17,968 --> 00:47:20,637
Chef & My Offal.

1208
00:47:21,772 --> 00:47:24,208
A MAKEOVER PROJECT FOR OFFAL

1209
00:47:24,575 --> 00:47:27,511
A CLASSY HOT POT DISH
TOPPED WITH BEEF SPINAL CORD

1210
00:47:28,145 --> 00:47:32,616
CHEF JUNG HO-YOUNG'S CHEF & MY OFFAL

1211
00:47:32,683 --> 00:47:36,653
-He topped it with the spinal cord later.
-Thank you.

1212
00:47:36,720 --> 00:47:40,224
First, try the spinal cord
with the morning glory stir-fry.

1213
00:47:40,290 --> 00:47:44,628
Right below that is the <i>doenjang</i> broth
made with ground monkfish liver.

1214
00:47:44,695 --> 00:47:47,731
-So try it with a piece of intestine.
-That broth was good.

1215
00:47:47,798 --> 00:47:49,132
Spinal cord and morning glory.

1216
00:47:49,199 --> 00:47:50,868
No sauce?

1217
00:47:50,934 --> 00:47:53,270
I've seasoned it with salt and sesame oil.

1218
00:47:53,337 --> 00:47:54,938
-So there's no sauce.
-And morning glory.

1219
00:47:55,005 --> 00:47:57,140
Yes, the greens are seasoned too.

1220
00:47:58,575 --> 00:48:00,143
ALL EYES ON HIM

1221
00:48:00,210 --> 00:48:01,912
The guy who loves offal.

1222
00:48:06,149 --> 00:48:08,886
TURNING INTO A CAUTIOUS MALTESE DOG

1223
00:48:08,952 --> 00:48:10,821
It's uncomfortable
to bear all this attention.

1224
00:48:13,490 --> 00:48:16,093
TAKING A BITE WHILE CURLED UP

1225
00:48:16,860 --> 00:48:21,031
It must be your first time
having beef spinal cord like this, right?

1226
00:48:21,098 --> 00:48:23,667
It tastes completely different
with morning glory.

1227
00:48:23,734 --> 00:48:25,035
A MAKEOVER FOR THE SPINAL CORD

1228
00:48:25,102 --> 00:48:28,071
Since you love offal very much already,

1229
00:48:28,138 --> 00:48:30,574
I wanted to make it in a different style.

1230
00:48:30,641 --> 00:48:31,875
Is it seasoned well?

1231
00:48:31,942 --> 00:48:33,710
-It's perfect.
-It's perfectly seasoned.

1232
00:48:33,777 --> 00:48:36,446
It's very important
that the food is seasoned perfectly.

1233
00:48:36,513 --> 00:48:37,447
APPROVED

1234
00:48:37,514 --> 00:48:39,149
ANXIOUS
OFF TO A SMOOTH START

1235
00:48:39,216 --> 00:48:40,617
I'll try the small intestines.

1236
00:48:40,684 --> 00:48:42,352
-A piece of small intestine.
-Intestines.

1237
00:48:42,419 --> 00:48:44,254
-Small intestines are delicious.
-They are.

1238
00:48:44,321 --> 00:48:46,657
The fatty filling was so good.

1239
00:48:47,057 --> 00:48:49,326
GETTING EVERYONE'S ATTENTION

1240
00:48:49,393 --> 00:48:51,295
FROM THE FRONT AND THE SIDES

1241
00:48:52,930 --> 00:48:55,032
THE CAUTIOUS DOG RETURNS

1242
00:48:55,098 --> 00:48:57,734
Don't be so cautious. You've even
surpassed ten million admissions.

1243
00:48:57,801 --> 00:49:00,137
It's the first time
everyone in the room looked at me.

1244
00:49:00,437 --> 00:49:02,105
YOU'RE THE MAIN CHARACTER TODAY

1245
00:49:02,172 --> 00:49:04,841
I'm sure many people
have given you attention already.

1246
00:49:04,908 --> 00:49:06,877
Don't you think
you're ducking down too low?

1247
00:49:06,944 --> 00:49:08,445
He's hiding behind that pot.

1248
00:49:08,512 --> 00:49:09,746
-You're a legend now.
-Gosh.

1249
00:49:09,813 --> 00:49:10,914
-Gosh.
-"Gosh."

1250
00:49:10,981 --> 00:49:12,382
BRIGHTENING UP

1251
00:49:12,449 --> 00:49:15,786
-Is it what you were looking for?
-Small intestines are perfect for this.

1252
00:49:16,119 --> 00:49:17,120
THEY MIX VERY WELL

1253
00:49:17,187 --> 00:49:18,689
<i>The texture is just right too.</i>

1254
00:49:20,257 --> 00:49:22,225
-I suggest that you try the soup.
-Sure.

1255
00:49:22,292 --> 00:49:24,061
-The soup.
-Made with <i>doenjang</i>

1256
00:49:24,127 --> 00:49:25,896
-and monkfish liver.
-That's right.

1257
00:49:25,963 --> 00:49:27,030
SLURPING ON THE SOUP

1258
00:49:27,764 --> 00:49:29,132
DEEPLY AMAZED

1259
00:49:29,499 --> 00:49:31,501
THE AMAZEMENT IS AS DEEP AS THE SOUP

1260
00:49:32,269 --> 00:49:33,236
ANOTHER SPOONFUL

1261
00:49:34,071 --> 00:49:35,305
THAT'S WHAT I'M TALKING ABOUT!

1262
00:49:35,372 --> 00:49:37,140
-It's warm and nice.
-The soup must taste good.

1263
00:49:37,207 --> 00:49:38,475
THE 3RD TASTE

1264
00:49:38,542 --> 00:49:41,778
-Is it different from other soups?
-It's definitely different.

1265
00:49:41,845 --> 00:49:45,182
I've never had <i>jeongol </i>like this one.

1266
00:49:45,248 --> 00:49:49,920
The soup tastes somewhat familiar,
but in the end, it's new.

1267
00:49:49,987 --> 00:49:52,689
It's even more delicious
to think of the ingredients as I eat it.

1268
00:49:52,756 --> 00:49:54,057
Is there any funky smell?

1269
00:49:54,124 --> 00:49:56,193
-No, and actually, I…
-No?

1270
00:49:57,160 --> 00:50:01,131
Many chefs do their best
to get rid of funky smells,

1271
00:50:01,198 --> 00:50:02,599
but I even enjoy that smell.

1272
00:50:02,666 --> 00:50:04,034
-So he likes offal.
-Basically,

1273
00:50:04,101 --> 00:50:06,603
he likes all smells, aromas,
and even something that stinks.

1274
00:50:06,670 --> 00:50:08,705
He likes everything that smells.

1275
00:50:08,772 --> 00:50:10,507
THE LAST BITE

1276
00:50:11,008 --> 00:50:12,743
-It's delicious.
-It is?

1277
00:50:12,809 --> 00:50:15,779
-Next, please try Chef Nam-no's dish.
-Chef Nam-no.

1278
00:50:15,846 --> 00:50:17,481
COLD POLLACK ROE AND BEEF SPINAL CORD

1279
00:50:17,547 --> 00:50:19,883
AND ASSORTED OFFAL JEONGOL

1280
00:50:20,150 --> 00:50:23,820
CHEF YOON NAM-NO'S SAVED YOU IN MY OFFAL

1281
00:50:24,421 --> 00:50:26,456
-Should he begin with the cold dish?
-Correct.

1282
00:50:26,523 --> 00:50:28,959
Which offal did you use for this one?

1283
00:50:29,026 --> 00:50:30,160
I mixed

1284
00:50:30,227 --> 00:50:33,397
<i>beef spinal cord with pollack roe,</i>
<i>which is also considered offal, right?</i>

1285
00:50:33,463 --> 00:50:35,632
I also topped it
with sea cucumber intestines.

1286
00:50:35,699 --> 00:50:37,801
ASSORTED OFFAL GIFT SET

1287
00:50:37,868 --> 00:50:39,870
It's a new kind of experience.

1288
00:50:39,936 --> 00:50:42,639
-And juiced tomatoes.
-With sea cucumber intestines.

1289
00:50:42,706 --> 00:50:43,840
He ate something long.

1290
00:50:45,008 --> 00:50:46,209
WIDE-EYED

1291
00:50:46,276 --> 00:50:49,980
-It's something that he'd love.
-He showed a big smile.

1292
00:50:50,047 --> 00:50:53,016
Sea cucumber intestines on top
was the smartest move.

1293
00:50:53,083 --> 00:50:54,584
-I see.
-He likes those things.

1294
00:50:54,651 --> 00:50:57,487
Otherwise, it would've been
something familiar,

1295
00:50:57,554 --> 00:51:00,991
<i>but that addition</i>
<i>just made the dish more flavorful.</i>

1296
00:51:01,058 --> 00:51:03,193
That was just the appetizer,

1297
00:51:03,260 --> 00:51:05,662
-but Nam-no already gets points.
-He seems to love it.

1298
00:51:06,830 --> 00:51:09,766
-He's taking huge bites.
-He likes it.

1299
00:51:09,833 --> 00:51:11,301
That means he really likes it.

1300
00:51:11,368 --> 00:51:14,771
I can tell that he loves it.

1301
00:51:15,072 --> 00:51:16,840
SAVORING

1302
00:51:16,907 --> 00:51:18,742
-It's good.
-It is.

1303
00:51:18,809 --> 00:51:20,110
He likes it.

1304
00:51:20,343 --> 00:51:21,545
PHEW

1305
00:51:21,611 --> 00:51:24,281
-Let's move on.
-Is there a ladle?

1306
00:51:24,347 --> 00:51:26,049
Back there, you said…

1307
00:51:26,116 --> 00:51:29,119
-You said that it smelled. What smell?
-I did.

1308
00:51:29,186 --> 00:51:30,620
-Like cilantro.
-That?

1309
00:51:30,687 --> 00:51:32,456
-He loves that smell.
-I do.

1310
00:51:33,023 --> 00:51:35,459
It must've been from the <i>chwinamul.</i>

1311
00:51:35,525 --> 00:51:36,827
Please pull that back

1312
00:51:36,893 --> 00:51:38,428
and dip the large intestines
in this sauce.

1313
00:51:38,495 --> 00:51:40,464
He's making use of it until the end.

1314
00:51:40,530 --> 00:51:42,132
Hang-jun liked it, so he's keeping it.

1315
00:51:42,432 --> 00:51:43,600
AND WHY NOT?

1316
00:51:43,667 --> 00:51:45,669
Nam-no seems a bit desperate.

1317
00:51:45,735 --> 00:51:46,870
-He's excited.
-He's in need.

1318
00:51:46,937 --> 00:51:48,171
The soup first.

1319
00:51:49,506 --> 00:51:50,640
What's the soup like?

1320
00:51:51,441 --> 00:51:52,409
That soup.

1321
00:51:52,476 --> 00:51:53,743
SLURP

1322
00:51:55,946 --> 00:51:59,149
It was a bit salty,
so he had to add some water.

1323
00:51:59,216 --> 00:52:01,718
-Is it good?
-It had a certain aroma.

1324
00:52:02,352 --> 00:52:05,021
It's the kind of flavor
I have never had before.

1325
00:52:07,057 --> 00:52:08,658
-But it's good.
-It is?

1326
00:52:08,725 --> 00:52:10,360
-I'm glad.
-It's something you've never had?

1327
00:52:10,694 --> 00:52:12,329
ARE THE INTESTINES DELICIOUS TOO?

1328
00:52:12,395 --> 00:52:15,332
-Was that <i>sundae?</i>
-<i>Pi-sundae,</i> Korean blood sausage.

1329
00:52:15,665 --> 00:52:17,200
ANXIOUS… NERVOUS…

1330
00:52:17,267 --> 00:52:18,101
Do you have to look?

1331
00:52:18,168 --> 00:52:19,769
WE WON'T LOOK, SO RELAX AND ENJOY

1332
00:52:19,836 --> 00:52:21,638
-We'll look away and chat.
-Let's chat.

1333
00:52:21,705 --> 00:52:23,206
We won't look.

1334
00:52:23,273 --> 00:52:24,508
Don't look that way.

1335
00:52:24,574 --> 00:52:26,109
He takes another bite while hiding.

1336
00:52:26,176 --> 00:52:27,944
He doesn't like attention.

1337
00:52:28,345 --> 00:52:30,380
A PIECE OF PI-SUNDAE GOES IN

1338
00:52:31,548 --> 00:52:33,049
GLANCES

1339
00:52:33,116 --> 00:52:34,351
He's still so cautious.

1340
00:52:34,417 --> 00:52:37,154
-He has an audience.
-And the soup.

1341
00:52:37,220 --> 00:52:38,989
-He took a huge bite.
-It's still hot!

1342
00:52:39,055 --> 00:52:41,525
-It's hot. Drink cold water.
-The <i>pi-sundae</i> is still hot.

1343
00:52:41,591 --> 00:52:42,726
-Gosh.
-"Gosh."

1344
00:52:42,792 --> 00:52:44,327
-This is good.
-It is?

1345
00:52:44,561 --> 00:52:46,830
ANOTHER BIG PRAISE

1346
00:52:46,897 --> 00:52:48,932
Let me try
the large intestine with <i>chwinamul.</i>

1347
00:52:48,999 --> 00:52:51,001
This time, I'll dip it in the sauce.

1348
00:52:51,067 --> 00:52:55,071
-He makes use of the tomato sauce.
-What's that like?

1349
00:52:56,072 --> 00:52:57,440
NODDING

1350
00:52:57,507 --> 00:52:59,309
-Was that good?
-It needs this sauce.

1351
00:52:59,509 --> 00:53:00,477
HEHE

1352
00:53:00,777 --> 00:53:01,778
I'M SO EXCITED♥

1353
00:53:01,845 --> 00:53:03,747
He did a great job with the sauce.

1354
00:53:03,813 --> 00:53:04,881
PRAISE MAKES HIM DANCE

1355
00:53:06,783 --> 00:53:08,752
Were there any other guests

1356
00:53:08,818 --> 00:53:11,888
who felt uncomfortable
with everyone's eyes on them?

1357
00:53:11,955 --> 00:53:13,723
Well, there were a few people,

1358
00:53:13,790 --> 00:53:15,192
but no one ate while hiding.

1359
00:53:16,993 --> 00:53:18,895
-There are small intestines too.
-Anything else?

1360
00:53:18,962 --> 00:53:20,630
DIPPING A PIECE OF SMALL INTESTINE

1361
00:53:20,697 --> 00:53:22,065
DIPPING A PIECE OF LARGE INTESTINE

1362
00:53:22,132 --> 00:53:24,601
-It must be great with the sea cucumber.
-He dips the large intestine.

1363
00:53:24,668 --> 00:53:26,469
-And <i>pi-sundae.</i>
-He's dipping everything.

1364
00:53:26,536 --> 00:53:28,138
He's dipping everything in the sauce.

1365
00:53:28,205 --> 00:53:31,575
-It must be great with everything.
-He must be so glad that he made it.

1366
00:53:31,641 --> 00:53:32,709
I'm so glad.

1367
00:53:33,376 --> 00:53:36,012
Does the flavor change with that sauce?

1368
00:53:36,079 --> 00:53:38,748
Yes, the meat still holds a bit of grease,

1369
00:53:38,815 --> 00:53:42,953
so this sauce helps
that greasy flavor disappear.

1370
00:53:43,019 --> 00:53:44,154
-So it balances it out.
-Yes.

1371
00:53:44,221 --> 00:53:46,356
VERY PLEASED

1372
00:53:46,423 --> 00:53:49,326
Would the two dishes be considered
different film genres?

1373
00:53:49,392 --> 00:53:51,294
-The ingredients are the same, right?
-Yes.

1374
00:53:51,361 --> 00:53:52,362
They're the same.

1375
00:53:52,429 --> 00:53:54,864
This one seems to be situated

1376
00:53:54,931 --> 00:53:59,469
-in a mountain village somewhere.
-A mountain village.

1377
00:53:59,536 --> 00:54:03,273
This one reminds me of a livestock farm.

1378
00:54:03,340 --> 00:54:06,409
-I see. Closer to civilization.
-Yes, that's right.

1379
00:54:06,476 --> 00:54:08,278
And now, let us have a taste too.

1380
00:54:08,345 --> 00:54:10,413
We'll begin with Chef Ho-young's dish.

1381
00:54:10,480 --> 00:54:12,882
Chef & My Offal.

1382
00:54:13,917 --> 00:54:15,485
I'LL TAKE ANOTHER BITE TOO

1383
00:54:16,853 --> 00:54:17,887
It's good.

1384
00:54:17,954 --> 00:54:20,790
It feels different to eat
beef spinal cord in this temperature.

1385
00:54:20,857 --> 00:54:22,692
-It's rich.
-Yes.

1386
00:54:22,759 --> 00:54:25,161
-It reminds me of <i>jeotgal</i>.
-It's monkfish liver.

1387
00:54:25,228 --> 00:54:27,364
A BITE, ANOTHER BITE

1388
00:54:28,398 --> 00:54:30,634
CAREFUL LIKE IT'S AN AUDITION

1389
00:54:31,368 --> 00:54:33,637
SOLEMN, STERN, SERIOUS

1390
00:54:34,004 --> 00:54:36,006
DID J. Y. PARK LIKE IT?

1391
00:54:36,072 --> 00:54:38,708
I produce singers, right?

1392
00:54:38,775 --> 00:54:41,344
What I do is hide their weakness
and bring out their strengths.

1393
00:54:41,411 --> 00:54:42,979
I don't actually create things.

1394
00:54:43,046 --> 00:54:45,815
And offal has such distinct pros and cons,

1395
00:54:45,882 --> 00:54:49,052
so it's a great dish if it brings out
the pros and hides the cons.

1396
00:54:49,119 --> 00:54:51,521
Beef spinal cord has its own flavor,

1397
00:54:51,588 --> 00:54:55,692
<i>and the ingredients and the seasoning</i>
<i>he added are in line with that flavor.</i>

1398
00:54:55,759 --> 00:55:00,463
Everything works in favor
of the spinal cord. It's fascinating.

1399
00:55:00,530 --> 00:55:01,765
ANXIOUS, BOWS

1400
00:55:01,831 --> 00:55:04,267
Jung-hwan says
the soup tastes like cutlassfish.

1401
00:55:04,334 --> 00:55:06,102
-It tastes like it.
-It's the monkfish.

1402
00:55:06,169 --> 00:55:07,304
-Is that it?
-The monkfish.

1403
00:55:07,370 --> 00:55:11,608
It tastes rich, as if he used
cutlassfish gut <i>jeotgal</i> for the soup.

1404
00:55:11,675 --> 00:55:12,942
But it's not too fishy.

1405
00:55:13,009 --> 00:55:15,278
He's famous
for his monkfish dishes, right?

1406
00:55:15,345 --> 00:55:17,981
-Monkfish Tiger.
-Monkfish Tiger returns.

1407
00:55:18,048 --> 00:55:18,948
Monkfish Tiger.

1408
00:55:19,015 --> 00:55:19,849
Director Yoo.

1409
00:55:19,916 --> 00:55:21,618
It looks like you're enjoying it.

1410
00:55:21,685 --> 00:55:23,620
It's delicious, but I'm getting worried.

1411
00:55:23,687 --> 00:55:26,222
-Why?
-How do you do this in 15 minutes?

1412
00:55:26,289 --> 00:55:28,758
Because he managed
to make this in 15 minutes?

1413
00:55:28,825 --> 00:55:31,361
Next, Chef Nam-no's dish,

1414
00:55:31,428 --> 00:55:32,996
Saved You in My Offal.

1415
00:55:33,229 --> 00:55:35,398
A BITE OF SEASONED POLLACK AND SPINAL CORD

1416
00:55:36,099 --> 00:55:37,634
-This is…
-It's like bulgogi.

1417
00:55:39,035 --> 00:55:40,003
This feels different.

1418
00:55:42,772 --> 00:55:45,141
WON'T STOP SCOOPING IT UP

1419
00:55:45,575 --> 00:55:47,043
CLEARED

1420
00:55:47,110 --> 00:55:48,545
He finished everything.

1421
00:55:48,611 --> 00:55:49,946
Did you like the other one too?

1422
00:55:50,013 --> 00:55:52,949
It wasn't the kind of taste
I expected from offal.

1423
00:55:53,016 --> 00:55:56,920
<i>But I can't believe how he made</i>
<i>something this put together</i>

1424
00:55:56,986 --> 00:55:58,621
in just 15 minutes.

1425
00:55:58,855 --> 00:56:00,423
HAPPY

1426
00:56:00,490 --> 00:56:02,992
I expected the tomato sauce
to taste refreshing and sour,

1427
00:56:03,059 --> 00:56:06,129
<i>but he brought out the umami</i>
<i>like that of a rich broth.</i>

1428
00:56:06,196 --> 00:56:07,630
It's salty and savory.

1429
00:56:07,697 --> 00:56:09,032
BROUGHT OUT THE POTENTIALS

1430
00:56:09,766 --> 00:56:11,534
The sourness

1431
00:56:11,601 --> 00:56:15,238
<i>of the tomato sauce</i>
<i>reminds me of gazpacho,</i>

1432
00:56:15,305 --> 00:56:17,841
which goes very well
with the greasy offal.

1433
00:56:17,907 --> 00:56:19,542
I see. They go well.

1434
00:56:19,609 --> 00:56:22,178
All right, then. It's time to choose.

1435
00:56:22,245 --> 00:56:24,681
<i>Press one to choose Nam-no,</i>

1436
00:56:24,748 --> 00:56:26,449
<i>and two to choose Ho-young.</i>

1437
00:56:27,250 --> 00:56:30,754
Which offal dish did you prefer?

1438
00:56:30,820 --> 00:56:32,756
You're not hiding your final choice.

1439
00:56:32,822 --> 00:56:34,290
SELECTIVE CAUTIOUSNESS?

1440
00:56:34,557 --> 00:56:35,892
OH, MY, MY

1441
00:56:35,959 --> 00:56:40,230
-He eats all hidden and chooses openly.
-Just like this?

1442
00:56:40,296 --> 00:56:42,065
He pressed a button.

1443
00:56:42,132 --> 00:56:45,301
Which one of them became the winner?

1444
00:56:45,368 --> 00:56:47,771
Let's find out who he chose.

1445
00:56:47,837 --> 00:56:49,305
Show us!

1446
00:56:49,372 --> 00:56:52,342
Which one of them will be
The Offal's Warden?

1447
00:56:52,409 --> 00:56:57,147
Will Ho-young beat Nam-no
and take his seventh star?

1448
00:56:57,213 --> 00:57:01,851
Or will Nam-no finally take a star
after four months?

1449
00:57:01,918 --> 00:57:03,753
Chang Hang-jun's choice!

1450
00:57:03,820 --> 00:57:05,622
Who did he side with?

1451
00:57:05,688 --> 00:57:08,124
Who's the winner?

1452
00:57:08,658 --> 00:57:11,528
Will it be Ho-young
who spent three years in Osaka? Or…

1453
00:57:11,594 --> 00:57:13,129
YOON NAM-NO WINS

1454
00:57:13,630 --> 00:57:15,532
CHEF YOON NAM-NO'S
SAVED YOU IN MY OFFAL WINS

1455
00:57:15,598 --> 00:57:17,767
Yoon Nam-no!

1456
00:57:17,834 --> 00:57:20,103
Nam-no finally wins a star!

1457
00:57:20,804 --> 00:57:21,938
It's been four months!

1458
00:57:22,672 --> 00:57:24,774
-The first in four months!
-Should I be happy?

1459
00:57:24,841 --> 00:57:26,876
Congratulations, Nam-no.

1460
00:57:26,943 --> 00:57:28,611
The legend in the world of offal.

1461
00:57:28,678 --> 00:57:30,480
The legend in the world of offal?

1462
00:57:30,547 --> 00:57:33,750
-I really liked that he used <i>chwinamul.</i>
<i>-Chwinamul.</i>

1463
00:57:33,817 --> 00:57:35,051
Yes, definitely.

1464
00:57:35,118 --> 00:57:39,823
I thought the <i>chwinamul</i> aroma
blended nicely with the intestines.

1465
00:57:39,889 --> 00:57:41,791
Also, above all,

1466
00:57:41,858 --> 00:57:44,027
without this sauce…

1467
00:57:44,861 --> 00:57:47,163
<i>-Yes.</i>
<i>-…he may not have won.</i>

1468
00:57:47,230 --> 00:57:49,466
This was the biggest kick.

1469
00:57:49,532 --> 00:57:52,769
I'm so glad that I got to taste
something different like this.

1470
00:57:52,836 --> 00:57:55,338
It looks like Nam-no is misty-eyed.

1471
00:57:55,405 --> 00:57:57,173
-Don't cry, Nam-no.
-Nam-no.

1472
00:57:57,240 --> 00:57:59,776
His lips are pouty.

1473
00:57:59,843 --> 00:58:02,011
You've broken your losing streak.

1474
00:58:02,078 --> 00:58:03,313
How do you feel?

1475
00:58:03,379 --> 00:58:05,014
I should stay true to myself

1476
00:58:05,081 --> 00:58:06,783
and cook without thinking too much.

1477
00:58:08,284 --> 00:58:09,819
I'll keep staying true to myself.

1478
00:58:09,886 --> 00:58:11,221
-Good.
-Okay.

1479
00:58:11,287 --> 00:58:13,990
-Hang-jun chose Chef Nam-no.
-Great round.

1480
00:58:14,057 --> 00:58:15,758
-Put a star on him!
-Thank you.

1481
00:58:15,825 --> 00:58:18,728
-He was chosen by Hang-jun!
-Thank you.

1482
00:58:18,795 --> 00:58:20,096
His second star!

1483
00:58:20,163 --> 00:58:22,098
-Thank you.
-Congratulations.

1484
00:58:22,966 --> 00:58:24,334
Hang-jun's choice.

1485
00:58:24,868 --> 00:58:29,105
<i>This is the second round of cook-off</i>
<i>with Hang-jun's ingredients.</i>

1486
00:58:29,172 --> 00:58:32,108
The Italian master-pupil
that bond over their bluffs,

1487
00:58:32,175 --> 00:58:34,477
Chef Choi Hyun-suk and Kwon Sung-jun.

1488
00:58:34,544 --> 00:58:35,578
They make a great duo.

1489
00:58:35,645 --> 00:58:38,348
The Chinese sister chefs
who bond over their lunacy,

1490
00:58:38,414 --> 00:58:41,084
Chef Yi Moon-jung and Park Eun-yeong.

1491
00:58:41,150 --> 00:58:42,652
They seem like actual sisters.

1492
00:58:42,719 --> 00:58:44,854
-You're the same height.
-We are.

1493
00:58:44,921 --> 00:58:46,155
And they're the master and the pupil.

1494
00:58:46,222 --> 00:58:47,924
I hear Chef Hyun-suk

1495
00:58:47,991 --> 00:58:50,126
is deeply concerned about this round

1496
00:58:50,193 --> 00:58:52,829
-because of his partner, Sung-jun.
-Why?

1497
00:58:52,896 --> 00:58:54,163
I'm the type

1498
00:58:54,230 --> 00:58:57,066
who can be the star player on the show

1499
00:58:57,133 --> 00:58:59,035
that scores the winning goal,

1500
00:58:59,102 --> 00:59:01,938
-but at times, I can assist well too.
-Right.

1501
00:59:02,005 --> 00:59:03,973
I can sacrifice myself to light the room,

1502
00:59:04,040 --> 00:59:05,108
like a candle.

1503
00:59:05,174 --> 00:59:08,011
-But he's like a light bulb.
-A light bulb?

1504
00:59:08,077 --> 00:59:10,580
And one of those fairy lights at that.

1505
00:59:10,647 --> 00:59:12,348
What's important is that he shines.

1506
00:59:12,415 --> 00:59:13,683
ONLY HE WANTS TO STAND OUT

1507
00:59:13,750 --> 00:59:15,752
Do you agree with what he said?

1508
00:59:16,319 --> 00:59:17,253
He's spot on.

1509
00:59:18,254 --> 00:59:19,889
At least he doesn't lie.

1510
00:59:19,956 --> 00:59:21,925
As always, I plan to shine all alone.

1511
00:59:21,991 --> 00:59:25,862
But are you ready to show
good teamwork with Chef Hyun-suk?

1512
00:59:25,929 --> 00:59:27,363
People say that men

1513
00:59:27,430 --> 00:59:30,266
never forget their first love
and their first teacher.

1514
00:59:30,333 --> 00:59:33,303
So with my first master,
Chef Hyun-suk, right here,

1515
00:59:33,369 --> 00:59:34,337
I feel very confident.

1516
00:59:34,404 --> 00:59:37,774
I guess I was his master
for a very short period.

1517
00:59:38,074 --> 00:59:39,309
UGH…

1518
00:59:39,375 --> 00:59:42,111
But he knows
exactly what he must do to shine,

1519
00:59:42,178 --> 00:59:44,414
so I plan to support him fully.

1520
00:59:44,480 --> 00:59:46,883
What about the Chinese sister chefs?

1521
00:59:46,950 --> 00:59:49,619
I often saw people saying things like,

1522
00:59:49,686 --> 00:59:53,489
"What's going on with the women
in the world of Chinese cuisine?"

1523
00:59:53,556 --> 00:59:55,058
These days, right?

1524
00:59:55,124 --> 00:59:58,995
-So yes, we are the crazy sisters.
-The crazy sisters.

1525
00:59:59,062 --> 00:59:59,929
We acknowledge that.

1526
00:59:59,996 --> 01:00:02,465
I've kept my eyes on them
and came to realize

1527
01:00:02,532 --> 01:00:04,734
-they're possessed by evil spirits.
-Evil spirits?

1528
01:00:04,801 --> 01:00:07,136
They keep bringing them out
whenever they cook.

1529
01:00:07,203 --> 01:00:09,439
But then, Chef Hyun-suk
often sprinkles salt, right?

1530
01:00:09,505 --> 01:00:12,875
I think we should throw it that way
to cleanse them from the evil spirits.

1531
01:00:12,942 --> 01:00:15,078
-I see.
-So we'll sprinkle salt on them.

1532
01:00:15,278 --> 01:00:16,613
HMPH!

1533
01:00:16,679 --> 01:00:21,351
Chef Eun-yeong, did you feel the pressure
to play as a team with Moon-jung?

1534
01:00:21,417 --> 01:00:23,820
I've been suffering
from three losses in a row,

1535
01:00:24,387 --> 01:00:27,056
whereas Chef Moon-jung
has won three times in a row.

1536
01:00:27,123 --> 01:00:29,592
So if we lose this round,
I have a feeling that it'll be my fault.

1537
01:00:29,659 --> 01:00:32,195
-So that's a bit of pressure.
-Yes, you'd be criticized.

1538
01:00:32,261 --> 01:00:34,797
Just enjoy the moment.

1539
01:00:34,864 --> 01:00:37,634
Winning the star isn't important to me.

1540
01:00:37,700 --> 01:00:39,569
-Okay.
-Keep it up.

1541
01:00:39,636 --> 01:00:40,970
-Give her a hug.
-Let's show them.

1542
01:00:41,037 --> 01:00:42,238
HUG, GLANCE

1543
01:00:42,305 --> 01:00:43,773
That was so heartwarming.

1544
01:00:43,840 --> 01:00:45,041
Chef Sung-jun.

1545
01:00:46,309 --> 01:00:47,143
CHUCKLE

1546
01:00:47,210 --> 01:00:49,145
I don't care about winning the star.

1547
01:00:49,212 --> 01:00:51,414
-I just want you to shine.
-Okay.

1548
01:00:51,948 --> 01:00:53,416
That's it?

1549
01:00:53,483 --> 01:00:54,617
I shall shine.

1550
01:00:56,219 --> 01:00:58,254
TEAM MOON-JUNG & EUN-YEONG:
PORK BELLY, BONELESS CHICKEN THIGHS,

1551
01:00:58,321 --> 01:01:00,390
CARROT, SICHUAN JJAJANG RAMYEON SOUP BASE,
PIG'S TROTTER, PERILLA LEAF, AND MORE

1552
01:01:00,456 --> 01:01:02,992
What we've prepared today is called

1553
01:01:03,059 --> 01:01:04,827
WISWB.

1554
01:01:04,894 --> 01:01:06,229
-WISWB?
-WISWB?

1555
01:01:06,295 --> 01:01:08,231
What matters
is the spirit that won't break?

1556
01:01:08,297 --> 01:01:12,602
What Matters Is that
Chinese Sister Chefs Won't Break.

1557
01:01:12,669 --> 01:01:15,238
What Matters Is that
Chinese Sister Chefs Won't Break, WISWB.

1558
01:01:15,304 --> 01:01:19,742
The King in <i>The King's Warden</i>

1559
01:01:19,809 --> 01:01:21,878
was in command of many,

1560
01:01:21,944 --> 01:01:23,079
but he…

1561
01:01:23,146 --> 01:01:25,314
SHE SUDDENLY BEGINS TO DANCE

1562
01:01:25,381 --> 01:01:27,316
She's doing that so suddenly.

1563
01:01:27,817 --> 01:01:30,520
SHE GOT INTO HER CHARACTER
DURING MOON-JUNG'S PRESENTATION…

1564
01:01:31,054 --> 01:01:33,389
BEGINS HER SOLO DANCE

1565
01:01:33,956 --> 01:01:34,957
-Please continue.
-He's…

1566
01:01:35,024 --> 01:01:36,826
-She's possessed.
-Did you plan this?

1567
01:01:36,893 --> 01:01:38,895
He's such a lonely man.

1568
01:01:38,961 --> 01:01:40,630
One day…

1569
01:01:40,997 --> 01:01:43,032
BOTH IN THEIR OWN TRANCES

1570
01:01:43,800 --> 01:01:46,069
EVEN DOING THE EXECUTIONER'S POSE

1571
01:01:46,135 --> 01:01:49,305
One day, I thought it'd be great
if he could sit with the people

1572
01:01:49,372 --> 01:01:52,075
-and have a drink with them.
-She's like an executioner.

1573
01:01:52,141 --> 01:01:53,643
-That's why…
-Gosh, Eun-yeong.

1574
01:01:53,710 --> 01:01:56,713
-That's the knife dance.
-She spurted water on the knife.

1575
01:01:56,779 --> 01:02:00,717
-We'll make Chinese wheat pancakes.
-Wheat pancakes.

1576
01:02:00,783 --> 01:02:03,119
-Wheat pancakes.
-We'll serve them with your favorites,

1577
01:02:03,186 --> 01:02:06,489
-pork belly, seasoned pig's trotters…
-Seasoned pig's trotters.

1578
01:02:06,556 --> 01:02:08,391
…and stir-fried chicken.

1579
01:02:08,458 --> 01:02:11,828
You'll have fun making different wraps.

1580
01:02:11,894 --> 01:02:14,097
-I'm looking forward to it.
-Also, we'll take down

1581
01:02:14,163 --> 01:02:16,032
those lousy Western cooks.

1582
01:02:16,099 --> 01:02:18,234
Then you can be called Chinese cooks!

1583
01:02:18,301 --> 01:02:19,969
That's awful. Lousy Western cooks?

1584
01:02:20,036 --> 01:02:22,605
That's one thing we hate to be called.

1585
01:02:22,672 --> 01:02:25,074
OTHER WESTERN COOKS ALSO GET TRIGGERED

1586
01:02:25,141 --> 01:02:27,343
They can't do anything without butter.

1587
01:02:27,410 --> 01:02:30,413
As Chinese cooks,
we prepared a good beating

1588
01:02:30,480 --> 01:02:33,483
-for those Western cooks.
-A good beating?

1589
01:02:33,549 --> 01:02:36,452
Despite the short amount of time,

1590
01:02:36,519 --> 01:02:38,554
-we'll also make a slushie.
-Slushie.

1591
01:02:38,621 --> 01:02:39,956
Without using a machine.

1592
01:02:40,022 --> 01:02:42,692
-Without a machine?
-She might use her knife.

1593
01:02:42,759 --> 01:02:46,696
The sisters will present our magic.

1594
01:02:47,296 --> 01:02:50,099
FULL OF EXPECTATION

1595
01:02:50,933 --> 01:02:52,969
TEAM HYUN-SUK & SUNG-JUN:
POMFRET, BLUE CRAB, SIRLOIN

1596
01:02:53,035 --> 01:02:55,104
PIG'S TROTTER, SWEET POTATO STEM,
CARROT, BREAD, ANCHOVY KAL-GUKSU SOUP BASE

1597
01:02:55,171 --> 01:02:58,407
Two Western cooks are up against them.
What are you two making?

1598
01:02:58,474 --> 01:02:59,842
-Your Majesty.
-Your Majesty.

1599
01:02:59,909 --> 01:03:02,612
It Is Time to Dine on Pasta.

1600
01:03:03,713 --> 01:03:06,382
I'm so worried about them!

1601
01:03:06,449 --> 01:03:09,252
I'm so worried.
They're already on different pages.

1602
01:03:09,318 --> 01:03:11,354
-Wait, I got it.
-"Your Majesty."

1603
01:03:11,420 --> 01:03:13,723
-"It Is Time to Dine on Pasta."
-"It Is Time to Dine on Pasta."

1604
01:03:13,790 --> 01:03:14,690
"Time to Dine on Pasta."

1605
01:03:14,757 --> 01:03:16,292
What are you making?

1606
01:03:16,359 --> 01:03:17,426
-Your Majesty.
-Your Majesty.

1607
01:03:17,493 --> 01:03:20,429
-It Is Time to Dine on Pasta.
-It Is Time to Dining Pasta.

1608
01:03:20,496 --> 01:03:22,832
It wasn't in sync. They should be exiled.

1609
01:03:23,166 --> 01:03:24,934
CHUCKLE

1610
01:03:25,001 --> 01:03:28,104
Your Majesty, It Is Time to Dine on Pasta.

1611
01:03:28,171 --> 01:03:29,572
<i>He went on an exile,</i>

1612
01:03:29,639 --> 01:03:32,175
<i>and he could only find Western cooks</i>
<i>in the neighborhood.</i>

1613
01:03:32,508 --> 01:03:33,743
INTRIGUED

1614
01:03:33,810 --> 01:03:36,145
And there, us Western cooks

1615
01:03:36,212 --> 01:03:38,648
-will beat the Chinese nobodies.
-Nobodies?

1616
01:03:38,714 --> 01:03:40,516
He just called you nobodies!

1617
01:03:40,583 --> 01:03:41,450
"Nobodies"?

1618
01:03:41,517 --> 01:03:43,352
What kind of pasta?

1619
01:03:43,419 --> 01:03:44,921
I want to challenge myself

1620
01:03:44,987 --> 01:03:47,356
and make fresh pasta within three minutes.

1621
01:03:47,423 --> 01:03:49,826
-In three minutes?
-Really?

1622
01:03:49,892 --> 01:03:51,761
-It'll be easy to pick.
-I'll make fresh pasta

1623
01:03:51,828 --> 01:03:53,663
to shine as the single fairy light.

1624
01:03:53,729 --> 01:03:55,231
To shine as the single fairy light?

1625
01:03:55,298 --> 01:03:59,202
-I'll make pasta similar to <i>gujeolpan.</i>
<i>-Gujeolpan?</i>

1626
01:03:59,268 --> 01:04:01,437
I'll make thin, fresh pasta
that'll be served cold

1627
01:04:01,504 --> 01:04:02,705
and add various toppings.

1628
01:04:02,772 --> 01:04:06,175
I'll use toppings like egg garnish
and sweet potato stems,

1629
01:04:06,242 --> 01:04:08,544
-like royal court cuisine.
-But it's pasta?

1630
01:04:08,611 --> 01:04:10,746
So pasta is your main dish?

1631
01:04:10,813 --> 01:04:12,815
-It's the appetizer.
-Pasta is the appetizer?

1632
01:04:12,882 --> 01:04:16,018
-I'll braise the pomfret as the main dish.
-Braised pomfret.

1633
01:04:16,085 --> 01:04:18,020
-It sounds good.
-It sounds great.

1634
01:04:18,087 --> 01:04:19,622
-Really?
-I'll bring out the tenderness,

1635
01:04:19,689 --> 01:04:24,560
while using Western cuisine techniques
to add different textures and inspire you.

1636
01:04:24,627 --> 01:04:27,230
And this braised pomfret
will taste like <i>ggotge-tang.</i>

1637
01:04:27,296 --> 01:04:29,498
-Whoa.
-But you won't make <i>ggotge-tang?</i>

1638
01:04:29,565 --> 01:04:30,867
-It'll taste like it?
-It'll be…

1639
01:04:30,933 --> 01:04:33,970
-Is he making bisque?
-…a nice dish for exhausted Hang-jun.

1640
01:04:34,036 --> 01:04:37,173
I want him to be inspired through this,
as well as be comforted

1641
01:04:37,240 --> 01:04:38,808
by the new experience.

1642
01:04:39,041 --> 01:04:40,209
MOVED

1643
01:04:40,276 --> 01:04:42,211
Let us begin the cook-off.

1644
01:04:42,278 --> 01:04:43,546
The timer, please.

1645
01:04:43,613 --> 01:04:46,582
Here to blow away
the bluffs of the Western cooks,

1646
01:04:46,649 --> 01:04:50,319
the lunatic and crazy
Chinese sister chefs,

1647
01:04:50,386 --> 01:04:52,889
Chef Yi Moon-jung and Park Eun-yeong.

1648
01:04:53,522 --> 01:04:54,957
They've come out well.

1649
01:04:55,024 --> 01:04:56,192
-They did.
-So well.

1650
01:04:56,259 --> 01:04:59,662
Here to cleanse
the lunacy of the Chinese sister chefs,

1651
01:04:59,729 --> 01:05:02,031
-the two Italian priests…
-I'll be like Sung-jun.

1652
01:05:02,098 --> 01:05:05,668
…Chef Choi Hyun-suk and Kwon Sung-jun.

1653
01:05:05,735 --> 01:05:09,272
Which dish will the exhausted Hang-jun
be more refreshed by?

1654
01:05:09,338 --> 01:05:10,640
It's a team round.

1655
01:05:10,706 --> 01:05:14,176
-Let the 15-minute cook-off begin!
-Let's go!

1656
01:05:14,243 --> 01:05:15,945
-Begin!
-Let's go!

1657
01:05:18,147 --> 01:05:19,415
HUGGING

1658
01:05:20,049 --> 01:05:21,651
TO THEIR POSITIONS AFTER THE HUG!

1659
01:05:22,485 --> 01:05:23,319
Let's go!

1660
01:05:23,386 --> 01:05:25,054
BOTH CHARGING FORWARD

1661
01:05:25,121 --> 01:05:27,590
He's prepping the pomfret first.

1662
01:05:27,657 --> 01:05:29,792
Hyun-suk's prepping the pomfret.

1663
01:05:29,859 --> 01:05:33,095
It's actually golden pompano,
which is much more expensive.

1664
01:05:33,162 --> 01:05:36,299
Hyun-suk cuts out
a piece of pomfret fillet.

1665
01:05:36,365 --> 01:05:37,333
All right.

1666
01:05:37,867 --> 01:05:39,468
WHAT'S THE FAIRY LIGHT UP TO?

1667
01:05:39,535 --> 01:05:41,437
-What did you put in?
-Sweet potato stems.

1668
01:05:41,504 --> 01:05:43,205
-What's that? Chives?
-Sweet potato stems.

1669
01:05:43,272 --> 01:05:45,174
-Sweet potatoes?
-Sweet potato stems.

1670
01:05:45,241 --> 01:05:46,642
Sweet potato stems.

1671
01:05:46,709 --> 01:05:48,110
WHAT'S NEXT?

1672
01:05:48,177 --> 01:05:50,079
They're using blue crabs too.

1673
01:05:50,146 --> 01:05:53,049
-<i>Ggotge-tang.</i>
-They're going into the oven.

1674
01:05:53,115 --> 01:05:54,250
-Bisque.
-By roasting.

1675
01:05:54,317 --> 01:05:56,552
-And then make broth?
-I think so.

1676
01:05:56,619 --> 01:05:58,454
They're probably making bisque.

1677
01:05:59,422 --> 01:06:00,656
I put the bread in the pan, Master.

1678
01:06:01,824 --> 01:06:02,825
TAPPING

1679
01:06:02,892 --> 01:06:03,726
EGG

1680
01:06:04,894 --> 01:06:06,362
MAKING THE PASTA DOUGH!

1681
01:06:06,429 --> 01:06:08,197
Chef Sung-jun, we must salt this.

1682
01:06:08,264 --> 01:06:09,498
-Chef Sung-jun.
-No, not now!

1683
01:06:09,565 --> 01:06:12,735
-Fine. I'll sprinkle it alone.
-I can't do it now.

1684
01:06:12,802 --> 01:06:13,669
ON HIS OWN

1685
01:06:13,736 --> 01:06:15,037
I'll sprinkle it alone.

1686
01:06:15,271 --> 01:06:16,872
CLEANSING THEM ALONE

1687
01:06:17,139 --> 01:06:18,607
MISSING TEAMWORK

1688
01:06:18,674 --> 01:06:21,811
They promised to sprinkle salt together,
but he had to make the dough.

1689
01:06:21,877 --> 01:06:26,182
Sung-jun was so sure
he'd make fresh pasta in three minutes.

1690
01:06:26,248 --> 01:06:28,684
He's doing a challenge of his own.

1691
01:06:28,751 --> 01:06:31,420
-Fresh pasta in three minutes.
-Three minutes.

1692
01:06:31,487 --> 01:06:34,190
-It's been a minute and ten seconds.
-Yes.

1693
01:06:36,058 --> 01:06:37,093
THREATENING BY SHARPENING

1694
01:06:37,159 --> 01:06:39,095
Moon-jung begins by sharpening her knife.

1695
01:06:39,161 --> 01:06:40,730
BEGINS TO PREP PORK BELLY!

1696
01:06:40,796 --> 01:06:43,432
Chef Moon-jung
seems to be working with pork belly.

1697
01:06:43,499 --> 01:06:45,034
She's really quick with her hands.

1698
01:06:45,101 --> 01:06:48,204
-Yes, Chef Moon-jung is really fast.
-She is.

1699
01:06:48,270 --> 01:06:50,506
That's her strong suit.

1700
01:06:50,773 --> 01:06:51,874
NEXT, BONELESS CHICKEN THIGHS!

1701
01:06:52,508 --> 01:06:54,810
1. JULIENNE PORK BELLY
AND BONELESS CHICKEN THIGHS

1702
01:06:55,745 --> 01:06:56,946
FINISHED IN NO TIME!

1703
01:06:57,179 --> 01:06:58,114
ON TO THE NEXT TASK!

1704
01:06:58,314 --> 01:07:01,350
CHEONGYANG PEPPER, GREEN ONION

1705
01:07:01,684 --> 01:07:04,587
CARROT, ONION

1706
01:07:04,920 --> 01:07:08,724
GARLIC, PERILLA LEAVES

1707
01:07:08,991 --> 01:07:10,993
She's so fast.

1708
01:07:11,060 --> 01:07:14,764
Chef Eun-yeong
is making dough with hot water.

1709
01:07:15,331 --> 01:07:18,067
Is Eun-yeong also making dough?

1710
01:07:18,134 --> 01:07:22,138
It must be for the wheat pancakes.
They said they'd make those.

1711
01:07:23,205 --> 01:07:25,775
-They're using soup base.
-<i>Ramyeon</i> soup base?

1712
01:07:25,841 --> 01:07:28,878
-They're using <i>ramyeon</i> soup base?
-Anchovy <i>kal-guksu</i> soup base.

1713
01:07:28,944 --> 01:07:30,546
-That's a good one.
-Anchovy <i>kal-guksu.</i>

1714
01:07:31,113 --> 01:07:33,783
You have a minute and a half
to finish making the noodles.

1715
01:07:34,517 --> 01:07:36,385
BEGINS TO FLATTEN THE DOUGH

1716
01:07:36,452 --> 01:07:38,554
Sung-jun, are you almost done?

1717
01:07:38,621 --> 01:07:40,189
I'm almost done.

1718
01:07:40,256 --> 01:07:42,958
Really? Are you really done with it?

1719
01:07:43,125 --> 01:07:44,560
THE BREAD SUNG-JUN HAD THROWN IN

1720
01:07:45,561 --> 01:07:46,495
Chef Sung-jun.

1721
01:07:46,562 --> 01:07:49,131
-Where's the piping tip?
-Over here.

1722
01:07:49,198 --> 01:07:50,132
-It's here.
-Okay.

1723
01:07:50,199 --> 01:07:52,168
You were supposed to do this,
but I'll do it.

1724
01:07:52,635 --> 01:07:55,104
FISHING FOR COMPLIMENTS

1725
01:07:55,404 --> 01:07:58,240
FORMERLY SUNG-JUN'S JOB

1726
01:07:58,307 --> 01:08:00,576
-Always making sure he gets the credit.
-Right.

1727
01:08:00,643 --> 01:08:03,412
-"Not my job, but I'll do it for you."
-Yes, exactly.

1728
01:08:03,479 --> 01:08:05,781
Otherwise, no one will know.

1729
01:08:05,848 --> 01:08:07,783
That wasn't actually his job.

1730
01:08:07,850 --> 01:08:10,619
Sung-jun has 45 seconds
to finish the noodles!

1731
01:08:10,686 --> 01:08:12,254
-Okay.
-Forty-five seconds.

1732
01:08:12,321 --> 01:08:13,622
I had to do something else.

1733
01:08:13,689 --> 01:08:14,924
It seems almost done,

1734
01:08:14,990 --> 01:08:17,760
-but he pledged to do it in three minutes.
-Yes, he said it.

1735
01:08:17,827 --> 01:08:20,296
Chef Eun-yeong,
are you making wheat pancakes?

1736
01:08:20,362 --> 01:08:22,765
-Yes, these are for the wheat pancakes.
-They look good.

1737
01:08:22,832 --> 01:08:24,967
-Looking perfect.
-You're right.

1738
01:08:25,034 --> 01:08:27,303
Chinese chefs are always good

1739
01:08:27,369 --> 01:08:30,272
-at making flour dough.
-The sizes are the same.

1740
01:08:30,539 --> 01:08:32,241
WHAT'S MOON-JUNG UP TO?

1741
01:08:32,308 --> 01:08:34,977
It looks like Moon-jung added
some <i>ramyeon</i> soup base to the meat.

1742
01:08:35,377 --> 01:08:36,412
OYSTER SAUCE

1743
01:08:36,479 --> 01:08:37,680
She's really quick.

1744
01:08:37,746 --> 01:08:40,616
I wonder what Moon-jung
and Eun-yeong will make as a team.

1745
01:08:40,683 --> 01:08:41,951
BEEF BULGOGI MARINADE

1746
01:08:42,017 --> 01:08:46,489
-It's almost time.
-The pasta, Sung-jun!

1747
01:08:46,555 --> 01:08:47,756
-Six. Five.
-Six. Five.

1748
01:08:47,823 --> 01:08:49,592
-Come on, Sung-jun. Six.
-Seven. Six.

1749
01:08:49,658 --> 01:08:50,626
I DID IT

1750
01:08:50,693 --> 01:08:53,596
It's ready!
That took less than three minutes.

1751
01:08:53,662 --> 01:08:56,499
He made fresh pasta noodles.

1752
01:08:56,565 --> 01:08:57,800
-Sung-jun.
-You did it.

1753
01:08:57,867 --> 01:08:59,969
The lone fairy light lit up.

1754
01:09:00,035 --> 01:09:01,036
WATCH ME BURN

1755
01:09:01,103 --> 01:09:03,906
-Wait, it's too early.
-I'll wash it with cold water.

1756
01:09:03,973 --> 01:09:05,508
-What?
-I'll wash it with cold water.

1757
01:09:05,574 --> 01:09:06,408
Okay.

1758
01:09:07,076 --> 01:09:11,046
What Chef Hyun-suk is doing
is a technique often used with potatoes.

1759
01:09:11,113 --> 01:09:12,781
-Sure.
-He's making scales

1760
01:09:12,848 --> 01:09:15,651
-with bread pieces.
-On top of the fish?

1761
01:09:15,718 --> 01:09:17,219
-Like the scales?
-You're right.

1762
01:09:17,286 --> 01:09:20,523
-They'll look like scales as it cooks.
-You're right.

1763
01:09:20,589 --> 01:09:22,658
Hang-jun is a filmmaker

1764
01:09:22,725 --> 01:09:26,162
who puts an emphasis on images,
so that can bring in extra points.

1765
01:09:26,228 --> 01:09:28,697
-The aesthetics are important.
-Yes.

1766
01:09:28,764 --> 01:09:31,033
-The visual beauty.
-Exactly.

1767
01:09:31,100 --> 01:09:33,269
Chef Eun-yeong is making wheat pancakes.

1768
01:09:33,335 --> 01:09:35,304
She's almost done with them too.

1769
01:09:35,371 --> 01:09:37,907
3. RUB SESAME OIL ON DOUGH DISCS,
STACK, THEN FLATTEN

1770
01:09:38,641 --> 01:09:41,310
Look how quick she is.

1771
01:09:41,377 --> 01:09:42,978
She's making pancakes quickly!

1772
01:09:43,045 --> 01:09:45,047
-Whoa!
-That's how you make them?

1773
01:09:45,114 --> 01:09:46,582
You're doing great!

1774
01:09:46,649 --> 01:09:47,983
SHE KNOWS HOW TO RAISE THE SPIRIT

1775
01:09:48,884 --> 01:09:52,521
Chef Eun-yeong knows
when to come in and shine

1776
01:09:52,588 --> 01:09:54,356
and when to step back and assist.

1777
01:09:54,423 --> 01:09:57,359
-When she must assist, she does that.
-She does.

1778
01:09:57,426 --> 01:09:58,661
-She quietly does her job.
-Yes.

1779
01:09:58,727 --> 01:10:00,262
-Ten minutes!
-Already?

1780
01:10:00,329 --> 01:10:02,765
What do we do? There's no time.

1781
01:10:02,831 --> 01:10:04,567
We don't have enough time.

1782
01:10:04,900 --> 01:10:06,535
CHOPPING THE INGREDIENTS
TO USE AS THE TOPPING!

1783
01:10:06,735 --> 01:10:10,139
5. JULIENNE SIRLOIN, CARROT

1784
01:10:10,206 --> 01:10:13,976
AND PIG'S TROTTERS

1785
01:10:15,144 --> 01:10:17,680
-Shouldn't you drain the pasta?
-I will!

1786
01:10:17,746 --> 01:10:19,248
-I'll do it.
-No, I got it.

1787
01:10:19,848 --> 01:10:22,418
I SHALL SHINE ALL ALONE

1788
01:10:22,484 --> 01:10:23,652
-Chef Sung-jun!
-Yes?

1789
01:10:23,719 --> 01:10:25,020
Let me know if you need help.

1790
01:10:25,087 --> 01:10:26,956
-Okay.
-I'll help you with anything.

1791
01:10:27,022 --> 01:10:29,858
He always demands compliments
after doing something that isn't his job.

1792
01:10:31,227 --> 01:10:33,963
GRILLING POMFRET WITH BREAD SCALES

1793
01:10:34,029 --> 01:10:34,997
Pot.

1794
01:10:35,664 --> 01:10:36,599
Where's the other pot?

1795
01:10:36,665 --> 01:10:38,200
-Which one?
-Where's the other pot?

1796
01:10:38,267 --> 01:10:39,702
-Pot? No idea.
-Is it over here?

1797
01:10:39,768 --> 01:10:41,804
COULDN'T CARE LESS IF IT ISN'T HIS JOB

1798
01:10:41,870 --> 01:10:43,739
-I found it.
-The pot.

1799
01:10:43,806 --> 01:10:45,708
POOR TEAMWORK,
JUST LIKE THEIR MISMATCHING LIMB LENGTHS

1800
01:10:45,975 --> 01:10:48,944
BAKED BLUE CRABS, OUT

1801
01:10:49,612 --> 01:10:50,613
I didn't use that pot.

1802
01:10:50,679 --> 01:10:52,047
Why is the heat so low?

1803
01:10:52,114 --> 01:10:53,749
QUICKLY COOKS THE CARROT

1804
01:10:54,250 --> 01:10:56,318
AND BEEF SIRLOIN

1805
01:10:56,619 --> 01:10:59,321
7. STIR-FRY BEEF SIRLOIN
WITH SOY SAUCE AND MINCED GARLIC

1806
01:11:00,022 --> 01:11:01,290
I need to make egg garnish.

1807
01:11:01,523 --> 01:11:03,158
WAS IN CHARGE OF EGG GARNISH

1808
01:11:03,492 --> 01:11:05,494
BUT FIRST, BLUE CRABS!

1809
01:11:06,095 --> 01:11:07,696
Nine minutes left!

1810
01:11:08,130 --> 01:11:09,798
EUN-YEONG BEGINS TO COOK THE PANCAKES!

1811
01:11:10,399 --> 01:11:13,335
Eun-yeong uses both hands.

1812
01:11:13,402 --> 01:11:15,337
USING BOTH HANDS

1813
01:11:15,404 --> 01:11:17,740
She's cooking two pieces at once.

1814
01:11:17,806 --> 01:11:18,741
She's really quick.

1815
01:11:18,807 --> 01:11:21,076
-The wheat pancakes look so good.
-Yes.

1816
01:11:21,143 --> 01:11:23,145
Pig's trotter?

1817
01:11:23,212 --> 01:11:25,648
-Pig's trotter.
-She's chopping it.

1818
01:11:25,714 --> 01:11:27,449
JULIENNING A PIG'S TROTTER TOO!

1819
01:11:27,816 --> 01:11:29,151
What's that for?

1820
01:11:29,218 --> 01:11:30,486
I'll season it.

1821
01:11:30,552 --> 01:11:32,421
They said they'd have him
make pancake wraps.

1822
01:11:33,255 --> 01:11:35,224
It'll become pancake filling.

1823
01:11:35,291 --> 01:11:37,026
-Moon-jung, I'm going to go.
-Wait.

1824
01:11:37,092 --> 01:11:38,694
Okay!

1825
01:11:38,761 --> 01:11:40,496
Go where, Eun-yeong?

1826
01:11:40,562 --> 01:11:42,665
-Here I go.
-Wait!

1827
01:11:42,731 --> 01:11:43,832
WHERE IS SHE GOING?

1828
01:11:43,899 --> 01:11:45,334
What are you doing?

1829
01:11:45,401 --> 01:11:47,803
Give them a good beating!

1830
01:11:47,870 --> 01:11:49,371
Give them a good

1831
01:11:50,639 --> 01:11:52,408
beating!

1832
01:11:53,242 --> 01:11:54,643
THE WHEAT PANCAKE SLAP

1833
01:11:54,877 --> 01:11:56,278
PERFECTLY SEPARATED INTO TWO

1834
01:11:56,345 --> 01:11:57,513
<i>Yaho!</i>

1835
01:11:57,579 --> 01:11:58,847
<i>Yaho!</i>

1836
01:11:59,214 --> 01:12:01,583
WHAT WAS THAT?

1837
01:12:01,650 --> 01:12:03,352
-Here we go again!
-Give him a good…

1838
01:12:03,419 --> 01:12:04,753
Give him a good

1839
01:12:05,788 --> 01:12:07,856
beating! Beat him!

1840
01:12:08,424 --> 01:12:09,458
She has to slap it.

1841
01:12:09,725 --> 01:12:11,260
WHEAT PANCAKE: STOP BEATING ME…

1842
01:12:11,327 --> 01:12:12,961
They're still stuck.

1843
01:12:13,028 --> 01:12:13,929
<i>Yaho.</i>

1844
01:12:14,296 --> 01:12:16,365
THE GYARU GHOST KEEPS POSSESSING HER

1845
01:12:16,432 --> 01:12:18,033
They make such a good team.

1846
01:12:18,100 --> 01:12:19,868
Yes, they're a great team.

1847
01:12:19,935 --> 01:12:21,937
-They have great teamwork.
-That's teamwork.

1848
01:12:22,004 --> 01:12:23,105
Right?

1849
01:12:23,172 --> 01:12:24,506
PUT A CLOTH ON TOP AND COOL

1850
01:12:24,773 --> 01:12:26,842
WHAT ABOUT TEAM WESTERN CUISINE
WITH ZERO TEAMWORK?

1851
01:12:27,176 --> 01:12:28,711
Chef, I think the fish is burning.

1852
01:12:31,080 --> 01:12:32,147
-What happened?
-No, Chef!

1853
01:12:32,715 --> 01:12:34,116
THE SCALES CAME OFF

1854
01:12:34,183 --> 01:12:35,751
No, I'll put them back on!

1855
01:12:35,818 --> 01:12:39,154
The fish scales
he tried so hard to stick on all fell off.

1856
01:12:39,221 --> 01:12:42,024
-The scales?
-The fish scales?

1857
01:12:42,358 --> 01:12:45,027
FALLING OFF…

1858
01:12:45,094 --> 01:12:47,363
I'll stick them back on later,
so be quiet!

1859
01:12:47,429 --> 01:12:49,765
-They all came off?
-They all did!

1860
01:12:49,832 --> 01:12:51,767
I will stick them back on, so be quiet!

1861
01:12:52,101 --> 01:12:54,002
POINTS FOR VISUALS: -10 POINTS

1862
01:12:54,069 --> 01:12:57,039
Why did you try
to make scales for the fish?

1863
01:12:57,106 --> 01:12:59,708
You said you'd make egg garnish.
Is it ready?

1864
01:12:59,775 --> 01:13:01,643
Egg garnish? I'm sorry. What now?

1865
01:13:01,710 --> 01:13:03,779
-Wait, Hyun-suk.
-What do we do?

1866
01:13:03,846 --> 01:13:05,180
I'll do it, Chef Hyun-suk.

1867
01:13:05,247 --> 01:13:07,015
-Let's do it together.
-Trust me.

1868
01:13:07,082 --> 01:13:09,818
-So the scales are gone?
-Yes, they're gone.

1869
01:13:09,885 --> 01:13:13,222
-The scales are charred!
-The scales!

1870
01:13:13,288 --> 01:13:15,290
-The scales.
-We're fine.

1871
01:13:15,357 --> 01:13:17,526
-We can do this.
-They're crunchy. Don't worry.

1872
01:13:17,593 --> 01:13:18,761
I'll just stick them on.

1873
01:13:19,561 --> 01:13:21,263
The scales look burnt.

1874
01:13:21,330 --> 01:13:23,298
-He puts them back on.
-I knew it.

1875
01:13:23,365 --> 01:13:25,701
Because they both burn brightly,

1876
01:13:25,768 --> 01:13:27,469
the scales got charred.

1877
01:13:27,536 --> 01:13:29,071
Six minutes and thirty seconds.

1878
01:13:30,105 --> 01:13:31,373
SUNG-JUN COVERS AND MAKES EGG GARNISH

1879
01:13:31,640 --> 01:13:33,609
TOSSING

1880
01:13:34,777 --> 01:13:36,979
-What's with the garnish?
-It looks odd.

1881
01:13:37,045 --> 01:13:39,014
Wait, what's with this?

1882
01:13:39,081 --> 01:13:40,115
I'll do the egg garnish.

1883
01:13:40,182 --> 01:13:41,250
You're going to do it?

1884
01:13:41,984 --> 01:13:44,186
HYUN-SUK IS IN CHARGE
OF THE EGG WHITE GARNISH

1885
01:13:44,653 --> 01:13:45,821
WHAT ABOUT SUNG-JUN'S EGG?

1886
01:13:46,121 --> 01:13:47,756
STARTING TO STICK TO THE PAN

1887
01:13:47,823 --> 01:13:49,725
It's an emergency.

1888
01:13:49,792 --> 01:13:52,194
-The egg garnish!
-The egg garnish is ruined!

1889
01:13:52,261 --> 01:13:54,062
-That was practice.
-It was ruined?

1890
01:13:54,129 --> 01:13:56,532
-It was a test.
-What test?

1891
01:13:56,598 --> 01:13:58,367
Lock them up!

1892
01:13:58,734 --> 01:14:01,336
IF IT WERE THE KING'S MEAL,
THEY'D BE IMPRISONED

1893
01:14:01,403 --> 01:14:04,239
-Lock them up in prison!
-They're heinous criminals!

1894
01:14:04,306 --> 01:14:05,507
Why are the scales dark?

1895
01:14:05,574 --> 01:14:06,442
Test success.

1896
01:14:09,211 --> 01:14:11,513
THANKFULLY,
THE WHITE GARNISH WAS A SUCCESS

1897
01:14:11,580 --> 01:14:13,048
The egg garnish.

1898
01:14:13,515 --> 01:14:14,817
TOSSING IT TO SUNG-JUN

1899
01:14:14,883 --> 01:14:16,084
Seven minutes.

1900
01:14:16,151 --> 01:14:17,286
Okay. We're fine.

1901
01:14:17,352 --> 01:14:18,854
Stay calm.

1902
01:14:18,921 --> 01:14:20,856
Season and toss it.

1903
01:14:20,923 --> 01:14:24,793
5. MIX PIG'S TROTTERS WITH BULDAK SAUCE,
VINEGAR, SUGAR, AND SESAME OIL

1904
01:14:24,860 --> 01:14:27,129
Eun-yeong is doing her part very well.

1905
01:14:27,396 --> 01:14:28,464
WHAT'S YI MOON-JUNG UP TO?

1906
01:14:28,897 --> 01:14:31,066
LOTS OF SALT ON ICE

1907
01:14:31,567 --> 01:14:34,036
AND A BOWL OVER THAT!

1908
01:14:37,005 --> 01:14:39,575
Moon-jung and Eun-yeong
are sailing smoothly.

1909
01:14:40,242 --> 01:14:42,044
Six minutes.

1910
01:14:43,111 --> 01:14:44,680
-What's in the bowl?
-What bowl?

1911
01:14:44,746 --> 01:14:46,582
-This one.
-This? It's the slushie.

1912
01:14:46,648 --> 01:14:47,683
-Slushie.
-Slushie.

1913
01:14:47,749 --> 01:14:48,717
They must make slushie too.

1914
01:14:48,784 --> 01:14:51,320
Wait, you aren't using a blender?

1915
01:14:51,386 --> 01:14:54,189
-They don't have one.
-How are you going to shave ice?

1916
01:14:54,256 --> 01:14:55,757
-Five minutes.
-Okay.

1917
01:14:55,824 --> 01:14:57,292
Please go check, Jung-hwan.

1918
01:14:57,359 --> 01:14:59,461
Chinese cooks versus Western cooks.

1919
01:14:59,528 --> 01:15:01,196
-Jeez.
-Isn't it insane?

1920
01:15:01,263 --> 01:15:03,131
This is awesome.

1921
01:15:03,699 --> 01:15:06,001
And I've been doing this weekly.

1922
01:15:06,068 --> 01:15:08,804
-The team round moves much faster.
-It's insane, isn't it?

1923
01:15:08,871 --> 01:15:10,539
This is amazing.

1924
01:15:11,773 --> 01:15:13,375
I don't think I can…

1925
01:15:13,442 --> 01:15:15,277
-Chef Moon-jung!
-I'll stir-fry now.

1926
01:15:15,344 --> 01:15:17,379
-Stir-fry?
-You'll stir-fry that?

1927
01:15:17,446 --> 01:15:18,914
They don't have enough time.

1928
01:15:18,981 --> 01:15:20,649
The meat. We're good.

1929
01:15:20,716 --> 01:15:22,017
THE MEAT THEY MARINATED

1930
01:15:22,084 --> 01:15:23,585
They seem busy.

1931
01:15:26,054 --> 01:15:27,289
What's this?

1932
01:15:27,356 --> 01:15:29,324
-Seasoned pig's trotter.
-Seasoned pig's trotter.

1933
01:15:29,391 --> 01:15:31,126
-It's the filling.
-For the wrap, right?

1934
01:15:31,193 --> 01:15:34,396
She's stir-frying here,
and the pancakes are coming along nicely.

1935
01:15:34,963 --> 01:15:36,265
Where's the strainer?

1936
01:15:36,331 --> 01:15:38,200
The strainer?

1937
01:15:38,267 --> 01:15:39,535
-I got it.
-Okay.

1938
01:15:41,670 --> 01:15:44,540
-It's an emergency. Let's hurry.
-It's an emergency.

1939
01:15:44,606 --> 01:15:46,341
9. BOIL DOWN BLUE CRAB BROTH WITH BUTTER

1940
01:15:46,408 --> 01:15:48,544
-Egg garnish.
-Egg garnish.

1941
01:15:49,611 --> 01:15:50,445
We only need a little.

1942
01:15:50,512 --> 01:15:51,947
Yes, we only need a bit.

1943
01:15:53,348 --> 01:15:55,450
CHOPPING EGG WHITE GARNISH
INTO THIN SLICES

1944
01:15:56,785 --> 01:15:58,353
JUST A TINY BIT

1945
01:15:58,420 --> 01:16:00,989
-The egg garnish.
-He ruined the first one, so it's a retry.

1946
01:16:01,490 --> 01:16:03,825
LOOKS LIKE QUAIL EGG GARNISH

1947
01:16:03,892 --> 01:16:05,661
Lock them up!

1948
01:16:05,727 --> 01:16:08,096
That's not an egg garnish!
It's a fried egg!

1949
01:16:08,163 --> 01:16:11,800
-It's a fried egg!
-That's not an egg garnish!

1950
01:16:11,867 --> 01:16:13,335
-It's not!
-Hyun-suk!

1951
01:16:13,402 --> 01:16:15,637
-It's not ruined.
-It's just a fried egg.

1952
01:16:15,704 --> 01:16:17,339
The garnish is only meant for His Majesty!

1953
01:16:17,406 --> 01:16:19,374
Hyun-suk insists it's not ruined.

1954
01:16:19,441 --> 01:16:23,545
-How do you call that egg garnish?
-That's a fried egg, not egg garnish!

1955
01:16:23,612 --> 01:16:24,947
Slow down.

1956
01:16:25,013 --> 01:16:26,615
The Chinese cooks have great teamwork.

1957
01:16:26,682 --> 01:16:28,917
-And they're quick.
-They work as a team

1958
01:16:28,984 --> 01:16:31,353
as they communicate.

1959
01:16:31,420 --> 01:16:34,122
Team Chinese is showing a better process.

1960
01:16:35,223 --> 01:16:36,658
ARGH!

1961
01:16:36,725 --> 01:16:37,559
ARGH!

1962
01:16:37,626 --> 01:16:40,028
She's stirring with one hand
and stir-frying with the other!

1963
01:16:40,095 --> 01:16:41,563
It's slowly freezing.

1964
01:16:41,630 --> 01:16:43,599
What? Really? It's starting to freeze?

1965
01:16:43,665 --> 01:16:46,234
-Can it freeze in time?
-It's freezing.

1966
01:16:47,703 --> 01:16:49,071
A TINY PIECE OF EGG YOLK GARNISH

1967
01:16:49,137 --> 01:16:49,972
It's a fried egg.

1968
01:16:50,038 --> 01:16:52,874
-How is that egg garnish?
-It is, once it's chopped!

1969
01:16:52,941 --> 01:16:55,043
He's chopping the fried egg
like it's a garnish!

1970
01:16:55,110 --> 01:16:56,411
Like it was an egg garnish!

1971
01:16:56,478 --> 01:16:57,679
The egg garnish looks great.

1972
01:16:57,946 --> 01:17:02,150
10. ADD OLIVE OIL AND SALT TO COOKED PASTA

1973
01:17:02,551 --> 01:17:04,886
TIME FOR MANTECARE

1974
01:17:05,687 --> 01:17:07,289
Now, the pasta.

1975
01:17:07,356 --> 01:17:09,224
-Pasta.
-Yes, separately.

1976
01:17:09,291 --> 01:17:10,525
Let me grill this over charcoal.

1977
01:17:10,592 --> 01:17:12,127
PLANS TO FLAME-GRILL THE CHICKEN!

1978
01:17:12,194 --> 01:17:13,795
You're using a lot of sauce.

1979
01:17:13,862 --> 01:17:16,732
She's stirring with one hand
and stir-frying with the other!

1980
01:17:16,798 --> 01:17:20,068
What are you doing? What's going on?

1981
01:17:20,502 --> 01:17:22,104
BURSTING INTO FLAMES

1982
01:17:22,170 --> 01:17:23,038
Chef Eun-yeong!

1983
01:17:23,105 --> 01:17:25,807
Simply starting a fire
can't make you shine!

1984
01:17:25,874 --> 01:17:28,744
I'm adding the smoky flavor!

1985
01:17:28,810 --> 01:17:30,746
This is the most complicated
kitchen situation

1986
01:17:30,812 --> 01:17:31,813
in the history of this show!

1987
01:17:33,048 --> 01:17:35,283
What's Eun-yeong cooking on the gridiron?

1988
01:17:35,350 --> 01:17:38,153
-Is this chicken?
-Boneless chicken thighs.

1989
01:17:38,220 --> 01:17:39,988
-Boneless chicken thighs.
-One minute.

1990
01:17:40,055 --> 01:17:41,556
THIS TEAM BEGINS TO PLATE THE DISHES

1991
01:17:43,492 --> 01:17:44,860
Chef Sung-jun, salt, please!

1992
01:17:45,260 --> 01:17:46,995
ATTACKING FIRST

1993
01:17:47,829 --> 01:17:49,031
-Salt!
-Take this!

1994
01:17:49,097 --> 01:17:50,065
Take this!

1995
01:17:50,399 --> 01:17:51,900
PFFT…

1996
01:17:52,100 --> 01:17:53,835
THEIR LENGTH DIFFERENCE IS JUST CRUEL

1997
01:17:53,902 --> 01:17:57,572
<i>Sung-jun's arm is so short</i>
<i>that he ended up salting Hyun-suk!</i>

1998
01:17:57,639 --> 01:17:59,174
They're too far away.

1999
01:17:59,574 --> 01:18:02,110
WHAT ABOUT THE SALTED SHAMANS?

2000
01:18:02,644 --> 01:18:03,545
SPIRALING

2001
01:18:03,612 --> 01:18:05,147
Do this.

2002
01:18:05,213 --> 01:18:07,649
-A minute and 30 seconds.
-Here we go, Moon-jung.

2003
01:18:07,716 --> 01:18:08,850
A minute and 30 seconds.

2004
01:18:08,917 --> 01:18:11,420
GOING, GOING, GOING…

2005
01:18:12,421 --> 01:18:14,456
CHANNELING A SPIRIT…

2006
01:18:14,690 --> 01:18:16,658
WE'RE SO SCARED…

2007
01:18:17,259 --> 01:18:18,660
You're doing great!

2008
01:18:18,727 --> 01:18:19,861
Keep going!

2009
01:18:19,928 --> 01:18:21,730
Go! Stay strong!

2010
01:18:21,797 --> 01:18:23,832
Switch with me. Good!

2011
01:18:23,899 --> 01:18:25,300
Okay. We're done!

2012
01:18:25,867 --> 01:18:27,769
-Plate the dishes!
-We're done!

2013
01:18:27,836 --> 01:18:31,073
-Finish first to take the upper hand.
-Bring me the dish.

2014
01:18:31,139 --> 01:18:33,642
Wait, what are you doing?

2015
01:18:33,709 --> 01:18:34,710
What is it?

2016
01:18:34,776 --> 01:18:36,044
POURING INFUSED BLUE CRAB SAUCE

2017
01:18:36,445 --> 01:18:38,013
WHAT ABOUT THE LONE FAIRY LIGHT?

2018
01:18:38,380 --> 01:18:41,550
ADDING TOPPINGS ON THE PASTA

2019
01:18:41,616 --> 01:18:42,851
-Are you done?
-Almost.

2020
01:18:42,918 --> 01:18:44,553
-This, in the middle.
-The sauce.

2021
01:18:44,619 --> 01:18:45,954
-I'll ring the bell.
-Okay.

2022
01:18:47,756 --> 01:18:49,691
-I'll ring it!
-Wait!

2023
01:18:49,758 --> 01:18:51,259
-I'll ring it now!
-Okay!

2024
01:18:51,326 --> 01:18:53,495
-Are you serious?
-Are you really done?

2025
01:18:53,562 --> 01:18:55,063
-Are you done?
-Almost done.

2026
01:18:55,130 --> 01:18:57,232
-They're about to finish.
-I'm done.

2027
01:18:57,299 --> 01:19:00,268
Team Hyun-suk and Sung-jun finishes first.

2028
01:19:00,335 --> 01:19:02,003
They still had one minute left.

2029
01:19:02,070 --> 01:19:04,239
They finished with one minute to spare.

2030
01:19:04,306 --> 01:19:06,074
It's okay.
Let's make use of the remaining time.

2031
01:19:06,141 --> 01:19:09,177
They're already going second,
so they're using the full 15 minutes.

2032
01:19:09,244 --> 01:19:10,812
Keep it up, Chinese chefs!

2033
01:19:10,879 --> 01:19:12,314
-Keep it up.
-Let's go!

2034
01:19:12,380 --> 01:19:13,849
-Go.
-We didn't need 15 minutes.

2035
01:19:13,915 --> 01:19:15,484
-Ten seconds!
-Eight!

2036
01:19:15,550 --> 01:19:18,720
-Seven. Six. Five.
-Seven. Six. Five.

2037
01:19:18,787 --> 01:19:20,856
-Four. Three.
-Four. Three.

2038
01:19:20,922 --> 01:19:23,125
-Two. One.
-Two. One.

2039
01:19:23,191 --> 01:19:25,794
-The end.
-We're done.

2040
01:19:26,128 --> 01:19:27,362
PESTERING WITH LONG LIMBS

2041
01:19:27,429 --> 01:19:28,430
I got it!

2042
01:19:28,697 --> 01:19:31,533
THE CHIHUAHUA WITH A SHARP TEMPER

2043
01:19:32,367 --> 01:19:34,035
Great job. It's all right.

2044
01:19:34,102 --> 01:19:35,003
BOTHERING WITH SHORT LIMBS

2045
01:19:35,270 --> 01:19:36,338
IT'S HECTIC UNTIL THE END

2046
01:19:37,472 --> 01:19:39,241
-And they're done.
-They're done!

2047
01:19:39,307 --> 01:19:40,175
Team Chinese is done.

2048
01:19:40,242 --> 01:19:42,577
-That was a hectic round.
-It's over.

2049
01:19:42,644 --> 01:19:44,546
Serve it with the ice bowl.

2050
01:19:44,613 --> 01:19:46,248
Can he drink it out of the straw?

2051
01:19:47,616 --> 01:19:49,217
SERVING THE ENTIRE BOWL

2052
01:19:49,284 --> 01:19:50,552
Are we on a vacation?

2053
01:19:52,788 --> 01:19:57,392
ON OUR WAY TO GIVE MORE ENERGY
TO EXHAUSTED HANG-JUN

2054
01:19:57,459 --> 01:19:58,460
It turned into slushie.

2055
01:19:58,527 --> 01:20:00,929
-How did it freeze?
-How did that happen?

2056
01:20:01,429 --> 01:20:03,231
AMAZED

2057
01:20:03,298 --> 01:20:07,903
Everything has been made
for exhausted Hang-jun.

2058
01:20:07,969 --> 01:20:10,672
That was a tense and dramatic round.

2059
01:20:10,739 --> 01:20:14,810
I never imagined cooking
could be so thrilling.

2060
01:20:14,876 --> 01:20:17,045
I was reminded of a horse race.

2061
01:20:17,112 --> 01:20:18,880
-Yes, a horse race.
-They only race forward.

2062
01:20:18,947 --> 01:20:21,149
"Horse number one. Horse number two."

2063
01:20:21,216 --> 01:20:23,852
Not only did they cook very quickly,
but they didn't forget

2064
01:20:23,919 --> 01:20:27,255
-to throw in humor in the process.
-Yes, that's what's important.

2065
01:20:27,322 --> 01:20:29,991
There were all kinds of emotions
and ups and downs.

2066
01:20:30,058 --> 01:20:32,661
They first burned something,
then found a way to cope with that.

2067
01:20:32,727 --> 01:20:35,564
-A renowned filmmaker would notice that.
-Yes.

2068
01:20:35,630 --> 01:20:38,233
Here's a thought I had
while watching this round.

2069
01:20:38,867 --> 01:20:41,336
"Yes, this is who we are as a people."

2070
01:20:42,270 --> 01:20:44,272
Is it strange

2071
01:20:44,339 --> 01:20:46,875
that I almost felt the patriotic hype
as I watched them?

2072
01:20:46,942 --> 01:20:48,176
You saw our potential.

2073
01:20:48,243 --> 01:20:49,811
<i>"This is who we are as a people."</i>

2074
01:20:49,878 --> 01:20:53,448
<i>They came through everything</i>
<i>despite the worst conditions.</i>

2075
01:20:53,515 --> 01:20:54,983
That was amazing.

2076
01:20:55,050 --> 01:20:58,220
All four sweated profusely

2077
01:20:58,286 --> 01:21:00,155
as they did their best.

2078
01:21:00,222 --> 01:21:02,924
-I can't wait to try these.
-You can't wait?

2079
01:21:02,991 --> 01:21:05,861
The two Western chefs finished first.

2080
01:21:06,194 --> 01:21:09,197
EGG YOLK, CARROT, SWEET POTATO STEM,
EGG WHITES, POLLACK ROE, SIRLOIN, TROTTERS

2081
01:21:09,264 --> 01:21:13,435
A FRESH PASTA DISH
PRESENTED LIKE GUJEOLPAN

2082
01:21:15,303 --> 01:21:17,739
BRAISED POMFRET
WITH PIECES OF BREAD SCALES

2083
01:21:18,373 --> 01:21:23,712
HYUN-SUK & SUNG-JUN'S
YOUR MAJESTY, IT IS TIME TO DINE ON PASTA

2084
01:21:23,778 --> 01:21:26,448
This one is the appetizer, right?

2085
01:21:26,514 --> 01:21:28,550
-Place them vertically aligned.
-Vertically.

2086
01:21:29,117 --> 01:21:30,986
SPINNING

2087
01:21:31,052 --> 01:21:32,721
-No, align the dishes vertically…
-The dishes.

2088
01:21:32,787 --> 01:21:35,223
…and place the pasta horizontally.

2089
01:21:35,290 --> 01:21:36,658
You've cooked long enough to know!

2090
01:21:37,359 --> 01:21:40,061
Okay. All right.

2091
01:21:40,128 --> 01:21:42,230
ONE MORE SERVING MISTAKE
AND THERE WILL BE TROUBLE

2092
01:21:42,297 --> 01:21:43,565
That's the appetizer.

2093
01:21:43,632 --> 01:21:46,368
-You can mix everything.
-Mix everything completely.

2094
01:21:46,434 --> 01:21:47,869
Mix everything?

2095
01:21:47,936 --> 01:21:51,306
They made cold pasta from scratch,
instead of using dried pasta.

2096
01:21:51,373 --> 01:21:54,309
-In three minutes.
-I wonder what that's like.

2097
01:21:54,376 --> 01:21:55,810
Pasta made faster than <i>ramyeon.</i>

2098
01:21:55,877 --> 01:21:58,713
-That's the appetizer.
-The pasta noodles.

2099
01:21:58,780 --> 01:22:00,181
<i>Gujeolpan </i>pasta.

2100
01:22:00,248 --> 01:22:02,984
He's really good at making pasta,
and he loves to eat it too.

2101
01:22:03,051 --> 01:22:04,786
-I should use chopsticks.
-Use chopsticks.

2102
01:22:05,820 --> 01:22:06,721
Your Majesty,

2103
01:22:06,788 --> 01:22:09,858
you'd better use chopsticks.

2104
01:22:09,925 --> 01:22:11,726
The King got exiled to a place

2105
01:22:11,793 --> 01:22:13,395
where only Western chefs lived.

2106
01:22:13,461 --> 01:22:15,964
-I love that backstory too.
-Sure.

2107
01:22:16,031 --> 01:22:17,799
At first, he didn't want it,

2108
01:22:17,866 --> 01:22:19,601
but he became too hungry.

2109
01:22:20,402 --> 01:22:22,437
If it's bad,
we'll send them back to their country.

2110
01:22:23,138 --> 01:22:26,174
So, Your Majesty, what do you think?

2111
01:22:26,241 --> 01:22:28,443
-Whoa.
-"Whoa."

2112
01:22:28,510 --> 01:22:30,378
The pasta noodles must be good.

2113
01:22:30,445 --> 01:22:34,816
I was just getting tired
and feeling drowsy,

2114
01:22:34,883 --> 01:22:37,819
-but this dish woke me up immediately.
-It did?

2115
01:22:37,886 --> 01:22:40,588
-The flavor that wakes you up.
-Yes.

2116
01:22:43,425 --> 01:22:44,859
He seems to like noodles.

2117
01:22:44,926 --> 01:22:45,961
MM-HMM

2118
01:22:46,027 --> 01:22:47,362
What's the pasta like?

2119
01:22:47,429 --> 01:22:48,596
It's excellent.

2120
01:22:48,663 --> 01:22:49,864
He made it in three minutes.

2121
01:22:49,931 --> 01:22:52,767
It's the kind of texture
that Koreans love.

2122
01:22:52,834 --> 01:22:56,237
I see. And it contains
many different ingredients.

2123
01:22:56,905 --> 01:23:00,575
AGAIN, ALL EYES ARE ON HIM

2124
01:23:01,977 --> 01:23:03,078
GLANCING

2125
01:23:04,813 --> 01:23:06,281
I keep getting conscious.

2126
01:23:06,348 --> 01:23:07,983
THE BIG SHOT FILMMAKER FEELS CAUTIOUS

2127
01:23:08,049 --> 01:23:10,885
Is there anything
they could've done better?

2128
01:23:10,952 --> 01:23:12,754
-If I must…
-If you must?

2129
01:23:12,821 --> 01:23:14,289
…point out a shortcoming,

2130
01:23:14,356 --> 01:23:15,390
it would be that

2131
01:23:15,457 --> 01:23:17,258
it needs a bit more umami.

2132
01:23:17,325 --> 01:23:18,526
Lash them!

2133
01:23:19,461 --> 01:23:22,163
The dish lacks umami!

2134
01:23:22,230 --> 01:23:24,933
Western cooks don't know how to add umami.

2135
01:23:25,000 --> 01:23:26,134
-Not yet.
-Not yet?

2136
01:23:26,201 --> 01:23:28,636
That's the appetizer,
so it can't be too strong.

2137
01:23:28,703 --> 01:23:30,171
It's just the appetizer.

2138
01:23:30,238 --> 01:23:33,308
-The umami.
-The main dish will explode with umami.

2139
01:23:34,175 --> 01:23:35,510
He saved it for the main dish.

2140
01:23:35,577 --> 01:23:36,945
-Let me…
-That's the main dish.

2141
01:23:37,012 --> 01:23:38,246
This is the main dish?

2142
01:23:38,313 --> 01:23:41,649
The main dish is a smaller portion
than the appetizer.

2143
01:23:42,350 --> 01:23:44,486
-Your Majesty, allow me to pour the sauce.
-The sauce.

2144
01:23:45,387 --> 01:23:46,654
Like that.

2145
01:23:46,721 --> 01:23:49,591
This is braised pomfret.

2146
01:23:49,657 --> 01:23:51,393
The portion reminds me

2147
01:23:51,459 --> 01:23:54,329
of a daycare kid's meal.

2148
01:23:54,396 --> 01:23:55,997
The scales

2149
01:23:56,064 --> 01:23:57,565
turned out like go stones.

2150
01:23:57,632 --> 01:24:00,035
They're go stones, not scales, right?

2151
01:24:00,101 --> 01:24:03,004
-He tried to depict fish scales.
-Not go stones?

2152
01:24:03,071 --> 01:24:04,439
Try it with the sauce.

2153
01:24:05,573 --> 01:24:08,543
They will be criminally charged
the moment he finds a bone.

2154
01:24:08,610 --> 01:24:09,677
We must lock them up.

2155
01:24:09,744 --> 01:24:11,446
-Gosh.
-Yes?

2156
01:24:11,846 --> 01:24:12,947
CURIOUS

2157
01:24:13,014 --> 01:24:15,550
-Your Majesty, do you like it?
-I knew it.

2158
01:24:15,617 --> 01:24:17,619
This dish

2159
01:24:17,685 --> 01:24:21,956
looked a little undersized when I saw it,

2160
01:24:22,023 --> 01:24:23,124
so I wasn't so impressed.

2161
01:24:23,191 --> 01:24:24,793
But the taste

2162
01:24:25,360 --> 01:24:27,295
-is just incredible.
-He's too good.

2163
01:24:27,362 --> 01:24:30,098
-Also, the scales.
-The bread.

2164
01:24:30,165 --> 01:24:32,033
They play a role in bringing out

2165
01:24:32,100 --> 01:24:34,069
the texture very nicely.

2166
01:24:34,135 --> 01:24:37,305
Pomfret tends to feel mushy when cooked,

2167
01:24:37,372 --> 01:24:38,373
but these add crunchiness.

2168
01:24:38,440 --> 01:24:42,243
The texture that boosts your mood
and makes the experience fun.

2169
01:24:42,310 --> 01:24:44,245
That was what Chef Hyun-suk was after.

2170
01:24:44,312 --> 01:24:45,146
Isn't it regular bread?

2171
01:24:45,213 --> 01:24:46,981
I wanted to create

2172
01:24:47,048 --> 01:24:48,683
different textures and flavors

2173
01:24:48,750 --> 01:24:52,320
within a single dish
to give you more inspiration.

2174
01:24:52,387 --> 01:24:54,155
STUMBLED OVER THE PRONUNCIATION

2175
01:24:54,222 --> 01:24:55,657
It's very delicious.

2176
01:24:55,723 --> 01:24:57,492
Next, WISWB.

2177
01:24:58,526 --> 01:25:02,330
FILL THE WHEAT PANCAKES WITH
PORK BELLY, CHICKEN, OR PIG'S TROTTER!

2178
01:25:04,299 --> 01:25:06,601
COLD SLUSHIE SERVED IN A BOWL

2179
01:25:07,535 --> 01:25:11,473
MOON-JUNG AND EUN-YEONG'S WISWB

2180
01:25:12,040 --> 01:25:15,510
Wait a second.
Did you mean to serve it like this?

2181
01:25:15,577 --> 01:25:16,678
Your Majesty.

2182
01:25:16,744 --> 01:25:18,546
Try to walk in your people's shoes

2183
01:25:18,613 --> 01:25:20,849
and drink it out of the straw,
straight from the bowl.

2184
01:25:20,915 --> 01:25:22,317
Straight from the bowl?

2185
01:25:22,383 --> 01:25:23,785
Straight from the bowl?

2186
01:25:24,252 --> 01:25:25,887
OH… VERY WELL!

2187
01:25:25,954 --> 01:25:29,791
Your Majesty, the people
are sipping it out of the bowl.

2188
01:25:29,858 --> 01:25:31,693
There were no straws back then.

2189
01:25:32,127 --> 01:25:33,862
HISTORICAL FALLACY

2190
01:25:33,928 --> 01:25:36,431
-So he's going to eat it with the pancake?
-The pancake.

2191
01:25:36,498 --> 01:25:38,700
-Chicken is the lightest and the cleanest.
-The center.

2192
01:25:38,766 --> 01:25:41,736
-The center. The pale one.
-The pale one in the center.

2193
01:25:41,803 --> 01:25:43,304
-This…
-Make a wrap with it first.

2194
01:25:43,371 --> 01:25:44,706
See if it's been seasoned well.

2195
01:25:44,772 --> 01:25:48,710
Try all three fillings,
then make a wrap with your favorite one.

2196
01:25:49,010 --> 01:25:50,678
A BITE OF JUST THE CHICKEN STIR-FRY

2197
01:25:50,745 --> 01:25:53,681
Eun-yeong worked very hard
stir-frying everything.

2198
01:25:53,748 --> 01:25:54,716
He's using both hands.

2199
01:25:54,782 --> 01:25:56,818
-It's delicious.
-He says it's delicious.

2200
01:25:57,719 --> 01:25:59,554
-Should he try everything?
-Sure.

2201
01:25:59,621 --> 01:26:00,722
What's that one?

2202
01:26:00,788 --> 01:26:03,358
What you grabbed is <i>jingjiang rousi,</i>
sauteed pork in sweet sauce.

2203
01:26:03,424 --> 01:26:07,362
-<i>Jingjiang rousi.</i>
-It's a meat stir-fry dish

2204
01:26:07,428 --> 01:26:09,130
cooked with <i>chunjang.</i>

2205
01:26:09,197 --> 01:26:11,933
But you didn't have <i>chunjang,</i>
so we improvised

2206
01:26:12,000 --> 01:26:15,537
<i>and used</i>
<i>Sichuan </i>jjajang ramyeon<i> soup base.</i>

2207
01:26:15,603 --> 01:26:17,572
<i>Jjajang ramyeon</i> soup base?

2208
01:26:17,639 --> 01:26:19,741
-Using <i>ramyeon </i>soup base is like cheating.
-I see.

2209
01:26:20,175 --> 01:26:22,143
THEY USED SOME TOO…

2210
01:26:22,210 --> 01:26:24,712
His Majesty enjoys <i>ramyeon</i> soup base.

2211
01:26:24,779 --> 01:26:26,281
That's why it's darker in color.

2212
01:26:26,347 --> 01:26:27,215
<i>Jingjiang rousi.</i>

2213
01:26:30,018 --> 01:26:31,653
Actually, Hang-jun is someone

2214
01:26:31,719 --> 01:26:34,122
who finds making wraps troublesome.

2215
01:26:34,455 --> 01:26:35,690
OH…

2216
01:26:35,757 --> 01:26:38,293
He doesn't like making wraps.

2217
01:26:39,260 --> 01:26:40,395
Ah-ha.

2218
01:26:40,962 --> 01:26:41,796
Whoa.

2219
01:26:42,230 --> 01:26:43,131
WHAT DO YOU THINK?

2220
01:26:43,198 --> 01:26:44,732
Is it all right? Are you pleased?

2221
01:26:44,799 --> 01:26:46,301
It's spicy and delicious.

2222
01:26:46,367 --> 01:26:47,402
-It's spicy?
-It is.

2223
01:26:47,468 --> 01:26:49,170
-It's the Sichuan version.
-Sichuan <i>jjajang ramyeon.</i>

2224
01:26:49,237 --> 01:26:51,039
It was the Sichuan version.

2225
01:26:51,105 --> 01:26:53,942
I saw you using Buldak sauce too.

2226
01:26:54,008 --> 01:26:56,945
It's in the <i>schweinshaxe,</i>
the pig's trotter dish.

2227
01:26:57,011 --> 01:26:58,379
-<i>Schweinshaxe?</i>
-That's <i>schweinshaxe?</i>

2228
01:26:58,446 --> 01:27:01,082
-That's <i>schweinshaxe?</i>
-<i>Schweinshaxe </i>for the King?

2229
01:27:01,149 --> 01:27:03,518
That is a German dish, Your Majesty.

2230
01:27:03,585 --> 01:27:05,453
But it's not all Buldak sauce.

2231
01:27:05,520 --> 01:27:08,456
<i>We just added a hint of it.</i>

2232
01:27:08,523 --> 01:27:09,824
It's probably spicy.

2233
01:27:09,891 --> 01:27:11,192
WHAT'S SEASONED PIG'S TROTTER LIKE?

2234
01:27:12,026 --> 01:27:13,027
He's about to eat it.

2235
01:27:13,595 --> 01:27:15,330
-This looks like the main dish.
-Wrap it.

2236
01:27:15,396 --> 01:27:17,966
-The pig's trotter.
-He'll like this one.

2237
01:27:18,566 --> 01:27:19,834
GULP

2238
01:27:19,901 --> 01:27:21,803
He seems pleased.

2239
01:27:21,869 --> 01:27:23,238
This <i>schweinshaxe</i> is the best.

2240
01:27:23,304 --> 01:27:25,240
-Among the three?
-Yes.

2241
01:27:25,306 --> 01:27:28,776
It's nicely spicy, and I love the texture.

2242
01:27:28,843 --> 01:27:32,747
<i>We used just the skin</i>
<i>to let you enjoy the chewy texture.</i>

2243
01:27:32,814 --> 01:27:35,183
Let me make a wrap
with all three fillings.

2244
01:27:35,250 --> 01:27:36,451
Please try it like that.

2245
01:27:36,517 --> 01:27:38,820
-You can mix them up too.
-It looks great.

2246
01:27:38,886 --> 01:27:39,988
However you'd like.

2247
01:27:40,888 --> 01:27:42,457
It's a Chinese-style dish.

2248
01:27:45,260 --> 01:27:46,928
-All three fillings.
-He has a tiny mouth.

2249
01:27:46,995 --> 01:27:48,663
-Yes, in one pancake.
-I do.

2250
01:27:50,131 --> 01:27:52,033
You don't have to eat the whole thing.

2251
01:27:52,100 --> 01:27:54,435
You can take small bites.

2252
01:27:54,502 --> 01:27:56,638
It's tough to keep his dignity
while eating that.

2253
01:27:56,704 --> 01:27:59,307
-Let's give him some time to chew.
-We should.

2254
01:27:59,374 --> 01:28:00,608
His mouth is full.

2255
01:28:00,675 --> 01:28:03,077
-I wonder what the mix is like.
-I wonder.

2256
01:28:03,144 --> 01:28:05,213
Does it taste like a German film?

2257
01:28:06,681 --> 01:28:11,085
There are all kinds of emotions,
love, friendship,

2258
01:28:11,152 --> 01:28:15,323
poetic justice, and everything.

2259
01:28:15,390 --> 01:28:16,424
But there's one thing.

2260
01:28:16,491 --> 01:28:19,460
It would've been better
if one characteristic stood out.

2261
01:28:19,827 --> 01:28:20,828
DISAPPOINTED

2262
01:28:20,895 --> 01:28:23,131
-Try the slushie too.
-Right, the slushie.

2263
01:28:23,865 --> 01:28:25,633
LOOKS REFRESHINGLY COLD

2264
01:28:25,700 --> 01:28:26,834
-The slushie.
-The slushie.

2265
01:28:26,901 --> 01:28:27,769
What did you use?

2266
01:28:27,835 --> 01:28:29,837
-Soju.
-Soju?

2267
01:28:29,904 --> 01:28:31,172
-It has alcohol?
-There's alcohol?

2268
01:28:31,239 --> 01:28:35,610
<i>Yes, I mixed soju, lemon-lime soda,</i>
<i>and blueberry juice.</i>

2269
01:28:35,677 --> 01:28:37,211
It should be a little sweet,

2270
01:28:37,278 --> 01:28:39,547
but we thought you would need
that sugar rush

2271
01:28:39,614 --> 01:28:42,250
-around this hour.
-Yes, I can feel the rush.

2272
01:28:43,451 --> 01:28:46,120
And how can I put this?

2273
01:28:46,721 --> 01:28:48,756
It's clearing up my head.

2274
01:28:48,823 --> 01:28:50,124
It must be the soju.

2275
01:28:50,191 --> 01:28:51,326
-Is that so?
-I guess so.

2276
01:28:51,626 --> 01:28:52,960
SOJU IS PERFECT AFTER AN EXHAUSTING DAY

2277
01:28:53,027 --> 01:28:54,162
-It's thanks to soju.
-It's soju.

2278
01:28:54,228 --> 01:28:56,731
I don't usually like
eating anything this sweet,

2279
01:28:56,798 --> 01:28:59,067
-but this one is good.
-That means…

2280
01:28:59,133 --> 01:29:01,202
How did the liquid turn into a slushie?

2281
01:29:01,269 --> 01:29:05,873
<i>Ice and salt create thermal conduction,</i>

2282
01:29:05,940 --> 01:29:08,743
<i>so it freezes the liquid</i>
<i>and creates a slushie.</i>

2283
01:29:08,810 --> 01:29:10,712
-It's science.
-It was scientific.

2284
01:29:10,778 --> 01:29:12,747
-It's time to choose.
-Yes.

2285
01:29:12,814 --> 01:29:13,881
It was a team round,

2286
01:29:13,948 --> 01:29:16,718
so two people will get one star each.

2287
01:29:16,784 --> 01:29:19,187
Please make a careful decision.

2288
01:29:19,253 --> 01:29:22,423
<i>Press one for Moon-jung and Eun-yeong,</i>
<i>Team Chinese Cuisine.</i>

2289
01:29:22,490 --> 01:29:25,159
<i>Press two for Hyun-suk and Sung-jun,</i>
<i>Team Western Cuisine.</i>

2290
01:29:25,226 --> 01:29:28,463
Make your decision and press the button!

2291
01:29:28,896 --> 01:29:29,931
PICKED ONE IMMEDIATELY

2292
01:29:29,997 --> 01:29:31,599
-I did.
-Already?

2293
01:29:31,666 --> 01:29:33,701
-Already?
-That was fast.

2294
01:29:33,768 --> 01:29:37,271
Are you the type
who usually decides quickly?

2295
01:29:37,338 --> 01:29:40,641
There are millions of decisions
to be made in my line of work.

2296
01:29:40,708 --> 01:29:42,610
The moment I step out of my car,

2297
01:29:42,677 --> 01:29:45,813
-the staff bombard me with questions.
-On what to do?

2298
01:29:45,880 --> 01:29:47,915
At most, I have to make
200 to 300 decisions a day,

2299
01:29:47,982 --> 01:29:49,384
and quickly too.

2300
01:29:49,450 --> 01:29:51,753
-Otherwise, the shoot gets delayed.
-Right.

2301
01:29:51,819 --> 01:29:53,654
Or was one side much better?

2302
01:29:54,455 --> 01:29:56,557
-It was very close.
-Very close.

2303
01:29:56,624 --> 01:29:58,192
-You just always decide quickly.
-Yes.

2304
01:29:58,259 --> 01:29:59,093
All right.

2305
01:29:59,160 --> 01:30:01,462
Let's find out the result. Show us!

2306
01:30:03,097 --> 01:30:05,633
A Dish for Exhausted Hang-jun.
Which side is it?

2307
01:30:05,700 --> 01:30:06,968
Is it Western cuisine

2308
01:30:07,034 --> 01:30:08,336
or Chinese cuisine?

2309
01:30:08,403 --> 01:30:10,972
Is it Hyun-suk and Sung-jun,
the master and the pupil?

2310
01:30:11,038 --> 01:30:13,374
or is it Moon-jung and Eun-yeong,
the sisters?

2311
01:30:13,441 --> 01:30:16,778
Which side is it?

2312
01:30:16,844 --> 01:30:18,946
Which dish was more comforting?

2313
01:30:20,181 --> 01:30:21,282
Who made you happier?

2314
01:30:21,349 --> 01:30:22,517
CHOI HYUN-SUK AND KWON SUNG-JUN WIN

2315
01:30:22,583 --> 01:30:24,752
KWON SUNG-JUN & CHOI HYUN-SUK WIN

2316
01:30:24,819 --> 01:30:26,921
Hyun-suk and Sung-jun!

2317
01:30:26,988 --> 01:30:28,990
-I knew it.
-It was Western cuisine.

2318
01:30:29,056 --> 01:30:30,158
That's my master.

2319
01:30:30,591 --> 01:30:32,894
THE BRIGHTLY DAZZLING LONE FAIRY LIGHT

2320
01:30:32,960 --> 01:30:34,095
Chef Hyun-suk sheds the light
solely on his student,

2321
01:30:34,162 --> 01:30:36,764
his junior chef and his pupil.

2322
01:30:37,198 --> 01:30:38,433
SHINE EVEN BRIGHTER

2323
01:30:38,499 --> 01:30:41,202
-He lets him take the spotlight.
-And he just takes it.

2324
01:30:41,269 --> 01:30:42,470
He's something.

2325
01:30:42,537 --> 01:30:44,405
What was the difference?

2326
01:30:44,472 --> 01:30:47,508
Chef Moon-jung and Eun-yeong's dish
was also very delicious.

2327
01:30:47,575 --> 01:30:49,143
-I see.
-Especially

2328
01:30:49,210 --> 01:30:51,045
-the <i>schweinshaxe.</i>
<i>-Schweinshaxe.</i>

2329
01:30:51,112 --> 01:30:53,614
If you served that dish alone,

2330
01:30:53,681 --> 01:30:55,349
-Rather?
-it could have changed

2331
01:30:55,416 --> 01:30:57,785
the entire plotline.

2332
01:30:57,852 --> 01:30:59,821
As for the Western cuisine,

2333
01:30:59,887 --> 01:31:01,222
I did not expect anything

2334
01:31:01,289 --> 01:31:03,691
-from that kid-sized pomfret.
-Kid-sized pomfret?

2335
01:31:03,758 --> 01:31:06,027
Were the scales made with bread?

2336
01:31:06,093 --> 01:31:08,529
Those scales gave the fish
such a nice spirit.

2337
01:31:08,596 --> 01:31:09,630
THANK YOU

2338
01:31:09,697 --> 01:31:11,566
-That was the key.
-The scales.

2339
01:31:11,632 --> 01:31:14,869
I'm not sure
who did more to win that star,

2340
01:31:14,936 --> 01:31:17,138
but let's hear from them.

2341
01:31:17,205 --> 01:31:19,440
We had such great teamwork today.

2342
01:31:19,507 --> 01:31:21,509
Also, we split up the task at first,

2343
01:31:21,576 --> 01:31:23,511
but unforeseen circumstances always arise.

2344
01:31:23,578 --> 01:31:26,881
The scales that he just complimented

2345
01:31:26,948 --> 01:31:30,451
were supposed to be cut out by Sung-jun,
but I did it.

2346
01:31:30,518 --> 01:31:33,387
I believe we won
because Sung-jun did a great job.

2347
01:31:33,754 --> 01:31:36,424
HE DOESN'T EVEN MEAN IT

2348
01:31:37,325 --> 01:31:39,460
That didn't quite add up.

2349
01:31:39,527 --> 01:31:42,563
Actually, Hang-jun said it accurately.

2350
01:31:42,630 --> 01:31:45,266
The fish dish could grab the attention

2351
01:31:45,333 --> 01:31:47,101
because I didn't
season the pasta too much.

2352
01:31:47,969 --> 01:31:49,103
You made that room.

2353
01:31:49,170 --> 01:31:50,638
I did.

2354
01:31:50,705 --> 01:31:52,573
It played its role as the appetizer.

2355
01:31:52,640 --> 01:31:55,309
When I just listen to you two,
you sound like a typical scammer duo.

2356
01:31:56,477 --> 01:31:58,779
You exaggerate so much.

2357
01:31:58,846 --> 01:32:02,350
This means the Western chefs have won.

2358
01:32:02,416 --> 01:32:03,684
Please put the stars on them.

2359
01:32:03,751 --> 01:32:05,453
-Wow.
-Congratulations.

2360
01:32:05,520 --> 01:32:07,355
-Thank you.
-Congrats.

2361
01:32:07,421 --> 01:32:09,123
-Thank you.
-One each for the two.

2362
01:32:10,091 --> 01:32:11,425
Smile a little.

2363
01:32:12,527 --> 01:32:14,428
-It's okay.
-I can't smile.

2364
01:32:14,495 --> 01:32:17,832
This means Hyun-suk now has eight stars

2365
01:32:17,899 --> 01:32:19,834
and Sung-jun has seven stars.

2366
01:32:21,335 --> 01:32:22,403
Eight wins, seven wins.

2367
01:32:23,104 --> 01:32:25,172
They chase right after the lead.
Congratulations!

2368
01:32:26,207 --> 01:32:28,543
-They have lots of stars.
-Western cuisine wins!

2369
01:32:30,745 --> 01:32:32,446
It's the 33rd year since his debut.

2370
01:32:32,513 --> 01:32:33,881
I'm in my best physical condition.

2371
01:32:33,948 --> 01:32:35,616
Where do you get this kind of energy?

2372
01:32:35,683 --> 01:32:38,386
I put all my money and effort
into my diet.

2373
01:32:38,452 --> 01:32:39,654
-We present his fridge!
-Fridge!

2374
01:32:39,720 --> 01:32:40,688
WOW

2375
01:32:40,755 --> 01:32:42,290
I'm already seeing
lots of "organic" labels.

2376
01:32:42,356 --> 01:32:44,058
His freezer's empty.

2377
01:32:44,125 --> 01:32:45,326
The thing is,

2378
01:32:45,393 --> 01:32:47,161
he's not prepared for an emergency.

2379
01:32:47,228 --> 01:32:48,996
He'll have to starve.

2380
01:32:49,063 --> 01:32:50,565
A cook-off for J. Y. Park.

2381
01:32:50,631 --> 01:32:52,400
There's fish, and there's meat.

2382
01:32:52,767 --> 01:32:53,734
IT ALREADY LOOKS HEALTHY

2383
01:32:53,801 --> 01:32:55,469
They're both desperate for a star.

2384
01:32:55,536 --> 01:32:57,104
-Wake up!
-Emergency!

2385
01:32:57,171 --> 01:32:58,105
It's an emergency.

2386
01:32:58,172 --> 01:32:59,407
Be quiet.

2387
01:32:59,473 --> 01:33:00,608
Sam's mad.

2388
01:33:00,675 --> 01:33:02,109
Poached eggs are great for pockets.

2389
01:33:02,176 --> 01:33:04,612
I'll use tenderloin
to let you sound tender.

2390
01:33:04,679 --> 01:33:06,047
He's dying to be funny.

2391
01:33:06,247 --> 01:33:07,582
THE ROAD TO KIM POONG IS NOT OVER

2392
